hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","46 - Chapter on bargaining with sellers. 1503 - Abu Yala said: Abdan narrated to us, Ziyad narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he would not bargain over three things: hire to Makkah, a slave to free, and the sacrifice."
"1802","47 - Chapter on reviving dead land. 1504 - Abu Bakr said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever revives dead land in which no Muslim has a right, it is his; and an unjust root has no right. Kathir is very weak."
"1803","Al-Tayalisi said: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Servants are Allah's servants, and lands are Allah's lands, and an unjust root has no right."
"1804","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Whoever revives a dead land, it is his."
"1805","48 - Chapter on endowments. 1507 - Musaddad: Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from one who heard Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he was asked about a man who dedicated something in the cause of Allah Almighty, may he divert it to another? He said: Spend it where its owner dedicated it. He said: By Allah, the cause of Allah is not that some of you strike the necks of others."
"1806","49 - Chapter on rewards. 1508 - Ishaq: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Rabah - that is Abdullah ibn Rabah - from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, who said: I came to Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) with runaways from Ayn al-Tamr - or he said: from al-Ayn - and he said: Rejoice in reward and spoils. He said: I said: This is the reward; what are the spoils? He said: Forty dirhams. And it is in Kufah."
"1807","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, from Abu Aishah al-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and mentioned a hadith, and in it: Whoever wrongs a hireling of his wage, his deeds are nullified and the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to him, and its fragrance is found from a journey of five hundred years."
"1808","Musaddad said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah and Abdullah ibn Dinar (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set the reward for a runaway slave, if taken outside the town, at ten dirhams."
"1809","14 - Book of Emancipation. 1511 - Al-Harith said, 1511: Ismail ibn Abi Ismail narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emancipation before ownership."
"1810","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: A woman freed a slave of hers, so Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said to her: Since you have freed him and did not stipulate his wealth, his wealth is his."
"1811","Abu Bakr said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ismail, from Abu Mijlaz, and he said: There was a slave owned by two men, and one of them freed his share, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) detained him until he sold some sheep."
"1812","Abu Bakr al-Samman narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad: There was a slave owned by two men, and one of them freed half of him, so his partner rode to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he wrote that he be valued at the highest value."
"1813","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim and al-Shabi, concerning a slave owned by two men, and one of them frees his share? He said: He guarantees a third of his price to his companion at a just valuation on the day he freed him."
"1814","Musaddad: Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Mujahid, who said: Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to a slave boy of his: O so-and-so, were it not that you are a child of adultery, I would have freed you."
"1815","Al-Humaydi said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Wasil, from Hilal, from a freedman of Banu Hashim, who said: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the worst of your slaves are the blacks; if they hunger they steal, and if they are sated they commit adultery. The hadith of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) on the virtue of emancipation has preceded. And that of Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) on emancipation at the beginning of the hadiths of the Prophets (peace be upon them). And the hadith of Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) on freeing ummahat al-awlad will come, Allah Almighty willing, in the chapter on treatment of women."
"1816","Al-Harith: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Mamar ibn Aban ibn Humran narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed us, who said: Urwah informed him: Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) was asked, and it was said to her: Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I give charity with the strap of my sandal is more beloved to me than that I free a child of adultery. Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: He heard badly and answered badly; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: That I give charity with the strap of my sandal is more beloved to me than that I command my slave-girl to commit adultery and free her child."
"1817","Ibn Abi Umar said: Bishr ibn Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, who said: I saw the mudabbar whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold."
"1818","Abu Bakr said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whatever a man frees from his slaves in his fatal illness is a bequest; if he wishes he may retract it."
"1819","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, that he saw no harm in a man retracting his emancipation."
"1820","Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: When a mukatab becomes bankrupt, debts are begun with."
"1821","Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: A mukatab of his became unable, so he returned him as a slave and kept what he had taken from him."
"1822","Hafs narrated to us, from al-Ashath, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: What they took from him is theirs - meaning: when he does not complete and is returned to slavery - so what was taken is theirs."
"1823","Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: When two installments follow consecutively and he does not pay his installments, he is returned to slavery."
"1824","Musaddad said: Al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): He judged concerning umm al-walad that she is not sold, nor given, nor inherited; her owner enjoys her while he lives, and when he dies she is free."
"1825","1 - Chapter on freeing a child of adultery. 1527 - Ishaq said: Muadh ibn Hisham informed us, my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, a man of our companions narrated to me, from a man, that a freedwoman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her a slave-girl, and that slave-girl bore a child from adultery, and she wanted to free her child, so she sought the counsel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That you give charity is better for you than that you free her; but keep her in service. I say: Its men are trustworthy, except the unnamed man, and his shaykh likewise."
"1826","15 - Book of Bequests. The hadith of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, and his bequest after his death, and its fulfillment through a dream vision, will come in full, Allah Almighty willing, in the virtues of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with him). 1528 - Musaddad said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Madan, who said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) explained that Allah Almighty has given you charity of a third of your wealth at your death."
"1827","Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Khalid ibn Abi Izzah, who said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) bequeathed a fifth, and said: I take from my wealth what Allah has made lawful from the fay of the Muslims."
"1828","Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Mujahid, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a caller who called on the day of the conquest of Makkah: There is no bequest for an heir; the child belongs to the bed; and no gift by a woman is valid except with her husband's permission."
"1829","Ishaq said: Yahya ibn al-Yaman informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth, from Shahr, from Asma bint Yazid - he said: I think she raised it - who said: There is no bequest for an heir."
"1830","1 - Chapter on the grandfather's inheritance. 1532 - Al-Harith: Ishaq - meaning al-Tabba - narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Isa ibn Abi Isa, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the grandfather a sixth of the wealth with a male child, and with one brother a half, and with two or more a third, and when there was no heir besides him he gave him the whole wealth."
"1831","1533/1 - Abu Bakr said: Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Iyad, from Abu Said (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We would give him inheritance in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning the grandfather."
"1832","1533/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr narrated to us with this."
"1833","1533/3 - Al-Bazzar said: Ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, Qabisah narrated to us. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know it with this wording from Abu Said (may Allah be pleased with him) except through this route, and I think Qabisah erred in his wording; what he had was: We would discharge it - meaning the fitr - and Qabisah was not followed in this."
"1834","2 - Chapter on the sister's son, freedman, and ally being of them. 1534 - Ishaq: Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us, Kathir - meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf - narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Admit the people to me, and admit none but Quraysh. They entered slipping in until the house was full. He said: Is there among you anyone not of you? They said: The sister's son, the freedman, and the ally. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sister's son is of them, their ally is of them, and their freedman is of them."
"1835","3 - Chapter on one who gives charity then it returns to him as inheritance. 1535 - Musaddad: Yazid - that is Ibn Zuray - narrated to us, Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi, from Abu al-Dahma, that he gave charity to his mother of a slave-girl of his whom he had contracted to free; then the mother died while a remainder of her contract remained. He said: I asked Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: You inherit your mother, and that you distribute her among her kin is more beloved to me. Sahih, mawquf."
"1836","4 - Chapter on those who die together, how they are inherited from. 1536 - Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith al-Awar, concerning people who drowned in a ship: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) made some of them inherit from others."
"1837","5 - Chapter on kalalah. 1537 - Ishaq: Jarir informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How do we give inheritance of kalalah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has not Allah Almighty already explained that? Then he recited: And if a man is inherited as kalalah, to its end. As if Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not understand, so Allah Almighty revealed: They ask you for a ruling; say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning kalalah, to the end of the verse. As if Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) did not understand, so he said to Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her): When you see ease from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ask him about it. She saw ease from him and asked him about it, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did your father write this for you? I do not think your father will ever know it. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: I do not think I shall ever know it, though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said what he said. Sahih if Ibn al-Musayyib heard it from Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1838","1538 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: It is not in the Book of Allah, nor in the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And they will all find it, and they will say: What is it? He will say: The inheritance of the sister with the daughter is half, though Allah Almighty said: If a man perishes having no child but has a sister, the verse."
"1839","1539 - Abu Yala said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man inherits his full brother to the exclusion of his paternal brothers."
"1840","1540 - Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, that he heard Murrah say concerning kalalah: I said to Murrah: Who doubts about kalalah? It is what is besides child and parent. He said: They doubt about the child."
"1841","6 - Chapter on inheritance of wala, and one at whose hands a man accepts Islam. 1541/1 - Ishaq: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, who said: Ali and al-Zubayr disputed before Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) concerning the freedmen of Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her). Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: She is my aunt, and I pay blood-money for her and inherit her. Al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: She is my mother, and I inherit her. Umar said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both): Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made wala follow inheritance?"
"1842","1541/2 - Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Hakam, the like of it, and he said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made wala follow inheritance? So he judged it for al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1843","1542 - Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Rashid ibn Sad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever a man accepts Islam at his hands, he is his freedman; he inherits him and pays on his behalf."
"1844","1543 - Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accepts Islam at the hands of a man, he is his freedman."
"1845","1544 - Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I asked Ibrahim about a Nabatean who accepts Islam and allies with a man. He said: He inherits him and pays blood-money for him."
"1846","7 - Chapter on one who held that a Muslim inherits from a disbeliever. 1545 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Amr ibn Kurdi, from Yahya ibn Yamar, who said: Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) would make the Muslim inherit from the disbeliever, and would not make the disbeliever inherit from the Muslim."
"1847","1546 - Musaddad said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Amr al-Wasiti, Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, who said: Two brothers disputed before Yahya ibn Yamar: a Jew and a Muslim. He made the Muslim inherit. It was said to him: Why did you make the Muslim inherit? He said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to me that a man narrated to him that two brothers disputed before Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him): a Jew and a Muslim. The Muslim said: My father was a Jew, and he had wealth and land, and my Islam did not harm me with him, except that he entrusted to me his wealth and land which I would cultivate and manage, and I would give charity, entertain guests, do good, and free slaves, and he would not fault me for that. Then he died. They came between me and his wealth and said: You have no right. So Muadh made the Muslim inherit."
"1848","1547 - Abu Waki narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Muslim does not inherit the disbeliever, unless he is his slave. And in a wording: Unless he is owned by him."
"1849","Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, from Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amrah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): There was found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a writing in it: Believers' blood is equal; the lowest of them strives to grant protection. No Muslim is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant. And people of two religions do not inherit from one another."
"1850","8 - Chapter on the inheritance of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 1549 - Abu Yala said: Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Malik narrated to us, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Prophet is not inherited from."
"1851","9 - Chapter on the inheritance of the apostate. 1550 - Ishaq: Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl ibn Ghazwan informed us, al-Walid ibn Jumay narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: When the apostate from Islam is killed, his child inherits him. This is disconnected, mawquf."
"1852","10 - Chapter on the inheritance of distant kin when there is no residuary. 1551 - Al-Harith: Abu Ubayd narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He asked Asim ibn Adiyy about Thabit ibn al-Dahdah: Do you know any lineage for him among you? They said: No; he is only an outsider among us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged his inheritance for his sister's son."
"1853","11 - Chapter on the inheritance of blood-money. 1552 - Abu Yala said: Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, who said: I read in the book of my grandfather Muawiyah ibn Amm Abi Qilabah, from the books of Abu Qilabah, and I found in it: This is what Muhammad ibn Thabit reminded al-Mughirah ibn Shubah of a judgment the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave: Blood-money among the heirs is inheritance according to the Book of Allah Almighty."
"1854","12 - Chapter: The killer does not inherit. 1553 - Abu Yala said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad and al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, and I copied it from the hadith of Abd al-Ala, Thawr (?) narrated to us - rather: Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, a man of them narrated to me, from a man called Adiyy, between whom and his two wives there was neighboring, and he threw a stone at one of them and killed her. He rode to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Tabuk, and asked him about the matter of the slain woman. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You pay her blood-money, but you do not inherit her."
"1855","16 - Book of Marriage. 1 - Chapter on women forbidden in marriage. 1554 - Ishaq said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Jafar, who said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) took Kab ibn Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him) by the hand and stood him between the two rows, and said to him: Narrate what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard him say: The brother's daughter and the sister's daughter through suckling are not lawful. This chain is weak; Jabir is al-Jufi, very weak, and Abu Jafar did not hear from Ali, nor from Kab (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1856","1555 - Abu Yala said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ibn Mawhab narrated to us, who said: I heard Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating, from Amrah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: There was found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she mentioned the hadith. She said: And at the end: A woman is not married upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt, and a woman does not travel three nights with one who is not a mahram."
"1857","1556 - Musaddad said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Amir al-Ahwal, from al-Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a slave-girl upon a free woman."
"1858","1557 - Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: Marrying a free woman upon a slave-girl is divorce of the slave-girl."
"1859","1558 - Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hasan, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Any man who marries while in ihram, we take his wife from him and do not validate his marriage."
"1860","1559 - Al-Harith said: Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hujr narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail ibn Hujr narrated to us, from his father, from Wail (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote a writing in it: There is no jalab, no janab, no wirat, and no shighar in Islam; every intoxicant is forbidden; and whoever practices ajba has practiced riba."
"1861","1560 - Abu Yala said: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Aban ibn Uthman, who said: One in ihram does not marry, nor propose for himself, nor for other than himself."
"1862","2 - Chapter on proposals. 1561 - Al-Harith: Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, from Abu Aishah al-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and mentioned the hadith, and in it: Whoever walks to arrange a lawful marriage until he joins them together, Allah Almighty grants him a thousand women of the houris, each woman in a palace of pearl and ruby, and for every step he takes or word he speaks in that, he has worship of a year, its nights in prayer and its days in fasting. And whoever walks to reconcile a woman and her husband has the reward of a thousand martyrs slain truly in the cause of Allah, and for every step, worship of a year, its fasting and its prayer."
"1863","3 - Chapter on dower and encouragement of it. 1562 - Ishaq said: al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, from Abu al-Harith, that is Jabir ibn al-Harith, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of you are those with the easiest dower. He said: Mujahid would say: If it is a dirham, it is lawful."
"1864","1563 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, Abu Farwah narrated to me, Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi narrated to me, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I met him and spoke to him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I went out with an uncle of mine on a journey, and he suffered sore feet, and said: Lend me your sandals. I said: I shall not lend them to you unless you marry me to your daughter. He said: I have married my daughter to you. He said: When we reached our family, he sent me my sandals and said: You have no wife with me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her; there is no good in her for you."
"1865","1564 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us, from Aban, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Never do two matters coincide but the more beloved of them to Allah Almighty is the easier of them."
"1866","1565 - Musaddad said: Isa, that is Ibn Yunus, narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, Abu Ubayd, chamberlain of Sulayman ibn Abd al-Malik, narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever marries a slave for Allah Almighty, marrying him only for Him, Allah Almighty crowns him in Paradise with a crown by which he is known. Mursal."
"1867","1566 - Abu Yala said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from al-Mujalid ibn Said, from al-Shabi, from Masruq, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) mounted the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Let me not know that dowers exceed four hundred dirhams. Then he descended. A woman of Quraysh confronted him and said: O Commander of the Believers, did you forbid people to exceed four hundred dirhams in their dowers? He said: Yes. She said: Did you not hear Allah Almighty say in the Quran: And you have given one of them a qintar, the verse? He said: O Allah, forgiveness; all people are more understanding than Umar. Then he returned, mounted, and said: O people, I had forbidden you to exceed four hundred dirhams in their dowers; whoever wishes to give of his wealth what he loves, or whoever is willing, let him do."
"1868","1567/1 - Al-Harith said: Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sin upon a man to marry with whatever of his wealth he wishes, little or much, when he calls witnesses."
"1869","1567/2 - Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us with it."
"1870","1568 - Abu Yala said: Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would divide sheep among his companions from charity, and a sheep would fall between two men, and one of them would say: Leave me your share that I may marry with it."
"1871","1569 - He said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah narrated to us, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deems lawful with a dirham has deemed lawful. And there will come, Allah willing, the hadith: No dower less than ten dirhams, in the chapter on guardians."
"1872","1570 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed me that his maternal aunt informed him, from a trustworthy woman, who said: While my father was on a campaign in Jahiliyyah and they had become parched, a man said: Who will give me his sandals and I shall marry him to the first daughter born to me? My father took off his sandals and threw them to him. A girl was born to the man and she grew up. My father said: Gather my family to me. He said: Bring the dower. He said: By Allah, I shall not increase you over what I gave you, for the two sandals. He said: By Allah, I shall not give her to you except for a dower. My father came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that. He said: Shall I not inform you of what is better than that? Leave her, so neither you swear falsely nor cause your companion to swear falsely. So my father left her. I say: Abu Dawud included it from this route up to his words: and she grew up. Then he referred the rest to the hadith of Maymunah bint Kardam."
"1873","4 - Chapter on choice in marriage. 1571 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), concerning a man who marries a woman with madness, leprosy, or vitiligo. He said: She is his wife; if he wishes he divorces, and if he wishes he keeps."
"1874","5 - Chapter on making emancipation the dower. 1572 - Ishaq said: Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, who said: Juwayriyah bint al-Harith said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your wives boast over me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not marry you; you are only a possession of the right hand. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did I not magnify your dower? Did I not free forty of your people?"
"1875","1573 - Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Hashim al-Kufi narrated to us, Kinanah, freedman of Safiyyah, narrated to us, from Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made her emancipation her dower; he dowered her with herself. And there will come, Allah Almighty willing, in the virtues the hadith of Razinah, her freedwoman, with what contradicts that."
"1876","6 - Chapter on consummation before the dower is given. 1574 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Talhah, from Khaythamah: A man married a woman and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared her trousseau, and he gave nothing. This is mursal. Sharik narrated it from Mansur, saying: from Talhah, from Khaythamah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her); Sharik connected it and Sufyan sent it as mursal. Abu Dawud and others included it from the hadith of Sharik."
"1877","7 - Chapter on encouraging attendance of marriages and holding them on Friday. 1575 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Numah, from his father, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever attends the marriage of a Muslim man, it is as if he fasted a day in the cause of Allah Almighty, and a day is seven hundred. And Abu Yala included: from the hadith of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Friday is a day of marriage and potency. It will come, Allah Almighty willing, in the beginning of creation."
"1878","8 - Chapter on the evil omen of women. 1576 - Al-Tayalisi said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul, who said: It was said to Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil omen is in three: in the house, the woman, and the horse. Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) did not memorize; for he entered while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying: May Allah destroy the Jews; they say: Evil omen is in three: in the house, the woman, and the horse. So he heard the end of the hadith and did not hear its beginning. Ahmad narrated its meaning through another route, from Abu Hassan, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1879","9 - Chapter on the marriage of one in ihram. 1577 - Ishaq said: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, my father narrated to us, I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating, from Ibn Abi Najih and Aban ibn Salih, that Mujahid narrated to them, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while in ihram, meaning Maymunah; and Ibn Umar and Said ibn al-Musayyib would deny that. I say: It is in the Sahih, from Ibn Abbas, and I mentioned it only for the denial of Ibn Umar."
"1880","10 - Chapter on just division and warning against withholding a woman's right. 1578 - Al-Harith: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, from Abu Aishah al-Sa'di, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and mentioned the hadith, and in it: Whoever wrongs a woman of her dower is with Allah Almighty an adulterer; and Allah Almighty will say to him on the Day of Resurrection: My servant, I married you upon My covenant, and you did not honor My covenant? So Allah Almighty undertakes seeking her right, and consumes all his good deeds; what remains of him, he is ordered to the Fire. And whoever has two wives and does not act justly between them in division of himself and his wealth will come on the Day of Resurrection shackled, his side bent, until he enters the Fire."
"1881","1579 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be carried to his wives while ill, and he would act justly among them in division."
"1882","1580 - Abu Yala said: Abu Musa narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended travel would cast lots among his wives, and the lot fell to Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) in the campaign of Banu al-Mustaliq."
"1883","11 - Chapter on consulting women about themselves and validating a father's marriage even if he did not consult her. 1581/1 - Al-Harith: Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibrahim ibn Salih, whose known name is Nuaym ibn al-Nahham, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had named him Salih, that he informed him, that Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): Propose for me the daughter of Salih. He said: He has orphans, and he would not prefer us over them. Abdullah went to his uncle Zayd ibn al-Khattab to propose for him, and he went with him to Salih and said: Abdullah ibn Umar has sent me to you to propose your daughter. He said: I have orphans, and I would not soil my flesh and raise your flesh. I call you to witness that I have married her to so-and-so. Her mother's inclination was toward Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abdullah ibn Umar proposed my daughter, and her father married her to an orphan in his care without consulting her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Salih and said: You married your daughter without consulting her? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Consult women about themselves, twice. Salih said: I did this only for what Ibn Umar dowers her; for she has from my wealth the like of what he gave her. 1581/2 - Isa ibn Hammad followed him, from al-Layth. Ibn al-Sakan included it in al-Sahabah through his route. And it is mursal, sahih in chain; Ibrahim did not attain hearing from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it is said he was born in his lifetime."
"1884","1582 - Abu Yala said: al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Fudayl Abu Muadh narrated to us, from Abu Hariz, from al-Shabi, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended to marry a woman of his women would say: So-and-so son of so-and-so mentions so-and-so daughter of so-and-so. Ahmad included it more fully than this through Abu Salamah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"1885","1583 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah ibn Muhajir or Muhajir ibn Ikrimah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between a virgin girl and her husband; her father had married her while she was unwilling. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he married one of his daughters would come to her chamber and say: So-and-so mentions so-and-so."
"1886","Chapter 12 - The marriage by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of any woman he wished without dowry, for himself and for others. 1584 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Abdurrahim ibn Harun al-Wasiti al-Ghassani narrated to us, Faid ibn Abdurrahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: By Allah, while we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, intense desire and hunger have destroyed me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bedouin, intense desire and hunger? He said: It is that. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, and the first woman you meet who has no husband, she is your wife. The Bedouin said: So I entered the palm grove of Banu al-Najjar, and there was a girl picking fruit into a basket, so I said to her: O owner of the basket, do you have a husband? She said: No. He said: Come down, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has married you to me. He said: So she came down, and I went with her to her house, and she said to her father: This Bedouin came to me while I was picking fruit into the basket, and asked me: Do you have a husband? I said: No, so he said: Come down, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has married you to me. So the father of the girl went out to the Bedouin, and the Bedouin said: What is the owner of the basket to you? He said: My daughter. He said: Does she have a husband? He said: No. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has married her to me. So the girl and the father of the girl went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does she have a husband? He said: No. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, prepare her trousseau well, then send her to him. So the father of the girl went and prepared his daughter and took good care of her, then sent with her dates and milk. She brought it to the house of the Bedouin, and the Bedouin went to his house and saw an adorned girl, and saw dates and milk, so he stood up to pray. When dawn broke he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the father of the girl came to his daughter, and she said: By Allah, he did not approach us, nor approach our dates or our milk! He said: So the father of the girl went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he called the Bedouin and said: O Bedouin, what prevented you from consummating with your wife? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I left your presence and entered the house and found an adorned girl, and saw dates and milk, so I felt obliged to spend my night until morning in worship, meaning in gratitude. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bedouin, go and consummate with your wife."
"1887","1585 - Abu Yala said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Kinanah ibn Nuaym al-Adawi, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Julaybib was a man of the Ansar, and he used to visit women and talk to them. Abu Barzah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So I said to my wife: Beware, Julaybib must not enter upon you! He said: And the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when one of them had a single woman, would not marry her off until they knew whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had any need concerning her or not. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to a man of the Ansar: O so-and-so, marry your daughter to me! He said: Gladly, and a delight to the eye! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not want her for myself. He said: For whom? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For Julaybib. He said: O Messenger of Allah, we will consult her mother. So he went and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is proposing for your daughter. She said: Gladly, and a delight to the eye! You would marry the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: He does not want her for himself. She said: For whom? He said: For Julaybib. She said: Alas! For Julaybib? No, by Allah, I will not give precedence to Julaybib. When her father stood to go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the girl said from behind her curtain to her parents: Who proposed for me to you? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Do you reject the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Hand me over to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he will never let me be lost. So her father went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Do with her as you wish, so he married her to Julaybib. Hammad said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah said to me: I said to Thabit: Do you know what he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for her? He said: O Allah, pour good upon them abundantly, and do not make their life one of toil and hardship! Thabit said: So he married her to him. I said: Rawh narrated it from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, and Daylam ibn Ghazwan followed him, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, and the narration of Hammad ibn Salamah is more authentic."
"1888","Chapter 13 - Avoiding touching an unrelated woman. 1586/1 - Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, that he heard Asma bint Yazid, may Allah be pleased with her, say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with some women, and he said to us: In what you are able? We said: O Messenger of Allah, take our pledge! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not shake hands with you; I only take from you what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took."
"1889","1586/2 - Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdurrahman narrated to us, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me, that he met Asma bint Yazid, may Allah be pleased with them. He said: She narrated to me: I only pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day the women pledged allegiance. She said: I extended my hand to pledge allegiance to him, so he withdrew his hand and said: I do not shake hands with women, but I only take from them by word."
"1890","1586/3 - Abu Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Mustaqim ibn Abdulmalik, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not shake hands with women."
"1891","Chapter 14 - Rulings of looking. 1587 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Amr ibn Saeed, who said: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: While I was circumambulating the House, I saw a woman and she impressed me. And it was said: The beauty of a woman you do not recognize does not harm you."
"1892","1588 - Abu Yala said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman informed us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to me, my grandfather narrated to me, who said: I heard Alqamah ibn al-Huwayrith al-Ghifari, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adultery of the two eyes is looking."
"1893","1589 - Al-Harith: Dawud narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Abu Aishah, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, and he mentioned a hadith, and in it: Whoever casts a forbidden glance at a woman, Allah will fill his eyes with Fire, then order him to the Fire; but if he lowers his gaze from her, Allah will fill his heart with His love and mercy, and order him to Paradise. And whoever shakes hands with a forbidden woman will come on the Day of Resurrection with his hands chained to his neck, then he will be ordered to the Fire; but if he jests with her, he will be detained for every word in this world for a thousand years. And in the hadith: And the anger of Allah is severe upon a married woman who fills her eyes with one other than her husband or one other than her unmarriageable kin; if she does that, Allah will nullify every deed she did, and if she lets another share his bed, it will be binding upon Allah Almighty to make her taste the Fire from the day she dies in her grave."
"1894","1590 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Sin is what disturbs hearts, and whatever glance occurs, Satan has a share of hope in it."
"1895","1591 - Abu Yala said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Bahili narrated to us, Abu Habib al-Ghanawi narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose eyes will not see the Fire on the Day of Resurrection: an eye that wept from fear of Allah Almighty, an eye that kept guard in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and an eye that lowered its gaze from what Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden."
"1896","1592 - Ishaq said: al-Mulai informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover your forelocks from us, O Umm Ayman."
"1897","1593 - Abu Bakr said: Qabisah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Saeed ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a Bedouin with a beautiful daughter of his, and the Bedouin kept presenting her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hoping he would marry her."
"1898","Chapter 15 - Recommendation concerning women. 1594 - Abu Yala said: Ibrahim ibn Saeed narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Ibn Buraydah, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best of you to their families."
"1899","Chapter 16 - Women have no say in marriage. 1595 - Musaddad said: Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from al-Qasim, who said: Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, married the daughter of Abdurrahman to al-Mundhir ibn az-Zubayr, so Abdurrahman said: Do you marry off the daughter of a man without his consent? So Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, became angry and said to al-Mundhir: Let him give her control of her affair? So he did, and they did not consider it anything."
"1900","Chapter 17 - A man offering his daughter to a righteous man to marry her. 1596 - Ishaq said: Sulayman ibn Harb informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Hafsah became widowed from her husband, and Uthman became widowed from Ruqayyah, so Umar passed by Uthman and said: Do you want Hafsah, for her waiting period has ended? He gave him no reply, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: I will marry Hafsah, and I will marry Uthman to her sister Umm Kulthum. So Umar said: How excellent. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Hafsah, and married Uthman to Umm Kulthum. I said: Its basis is in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Umar, from Umar."
"1901","Chapter 18 - Marrying virgins. 1597/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Dawud ibn az-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from ar-Rabi ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from Kab ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we camped one night, then we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the morning, and he began asking man by man: Have you married, O so-and-so? Have you married, O so-and-so? Then he said: Have you married, O Kab? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A virgin or a previously married woman? I said: A previously married woman. He said: Why not a virgin whom you bite playfully and who bites you?"
"1902","1597/2 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Amr ibn an-Numan narrated to us, Musa ibn Dihqan narrated to us, ar-Rabi ibn Kab ibn Ujrah narrated to me, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: O so-and-so, have you married? He said: No. He said: Then he said to me: Have you married? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a previously married woman? Then he mentioned it."
"1903","1597/3 - He said: And Abdurrahman ibn Jabalah narrated to us, Amr ibn an-Numan narrated to us, then he mentioned it, but it does not contain: from his father."
"1904","1908 - Abdan narrated to us, Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, who said: al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, disliked marrying off the orphan boy and orphan girl until they reach puberty."
"1905","Chapter 19 - The scheming of women, and pardoning what comes from a jealous one in her jealousy. 1599 - Abu Yala said: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, from his father, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he took his wives with him, may Allah be pleased with them. She said: My baggage was light, so it was on a fast camel. The baggage of Safiyyah bint Huyayy, may Allah be pleased with her, was heavy, on a heavy slow camel that held back the caravan, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Transfer the baggage of Aisha onto the camel of Safiyyah, and transfer the baggage of Safiyyah onto the camel of Aisha, so that the caravan may proceed. When I saw that, Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I said: O refuge in Allah! This Jewess has overcome the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Abdullah, your baggage was light, and the baggage of Safiyyah was heavy, so the caravan was delayed, so we transferred her baggage onto your camel, and transferred your baggage onto her camel! She said: I said: Do you not claim you are the Messenger of Allah? She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: Are you doubting me, O Umm Abdullah? She said: I said: Do you not claim you are the Messenger of Allah? Then why are you not just? Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, heard me, and he had sharpness, meaning severity, so he came to me and slapped my face, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Abu Bakr. He said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The jealous one does not distinguish the bottom of the valley from its top. The hadith of Razinah, may Allah be pleased with her, will come, Allah willing, in the chapter of joking in the Book of Manners."
"1906","1600 - Abu Yala said: al-Musajji ibn Musab al-Basri narrated to us, Rabiah narrated to me, Umayyah narrated to me, from Maymunah bint Abi Asib, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: A woman from Jurash came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a camel, and called: O Aisha, help me with a supplication from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that will calm me or make me well by it! And he said to her: Place your right hand on your heart and wipe it, and say: In the name of Allah, O Allah, treat me with Your cure, heal me with Your healing, enrich me with Your richness and bounty apart from others, and remove Your harm from me. Rabiah said: So I supplicated with it and found it good. He said: I think Rabiah said in this hadith: The woman was jealous."
"1907","Chapter 20 - Living with women. 1601/1 - Ishaq: I said to Abu Usamah: Did Abu Talq ibn Hanzalah narrate to you, my father narrated to me, from Aws ibn Thurayb ath-Thalabi, who said: I hired out Abdullah ibn Jarir in Hajj, and he came to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who asked him about things, and among what he asked him he said: How did you find your wives? He said: O Commander of the Believers, I cannot kiss one of them except on her day without her suspecting me, and I do not go out for a need without her saying: You were with so-and-so, you were with so-and-so. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Many of them do not believe in Allah, nor trust the believers, yet one of them may be attending to the need of one of them, or go to the market and buy something needed for one of them, and she suspects him. So Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Commander of the Believers, did you not know that Ibrahim, the close friend of the Merciful, complained to Allah Almighty about sharpness in the character of Sarah, so He said to him: Woman is like a rib; if you leave her she remains crooked, and if you straighten her she breaks; so enjoy her despite what is in her. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, struck between the shoulders of Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: Allah has certainly placed no little knowledge in your heart, O Ibn Masud? So Abu Usamah affirmed it, and said: Yes."
"1908","1601/2 - Ishaq also said: al-Makhzumi informed us, Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Talq narrated to us, my father Hanzalah ibn Nuaym narrated to me, Thurayb or Ibn Thurayb narrated to me, who said: I hired out in Hajj and entered the mosque, and Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was sitting, and Jarir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, among people, so Umar said to Jarir, then he mentioned the same, and said: Sharpness in the character of Sarah."
"1909","1601/3 - Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed me, from ar-Rukayn and Abu Talq, from a man, from Jarir, one of them adding over the other, and he mentioned similar to this."
"1910","1602/1 - Abu Bakr said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and he mentioned a long hadith in it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, women are captives with you; you took them by the trust of Allah Almighty, and you made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. You have a right over them, and they have a right over you. Part of your right is that they not let those you dislike tread your beds, nor disobey you in what is right. If they do so, then they have their provision and clothing in a customary manner, and when you strike, strike without severity, the hadith."
"1911","1602/2 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."
"1912","1603 - Ishaq said: al-Aqadi informed us, Sulayman, who is Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Safiyyah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when no one among people was more hateful to me than him, and he kept saying: Your people did such and such, and did such and such, and I did not rise from that sitting until no one was more beloved to me than him. I said: It is mursal."
"1913","1604 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah narrated to us, from Abu Aishah, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Whoever has intercourse with a woman in her anus, or with a man, or a boy, will come on the Day of Resurrection stinking worse than carrion, the hadith. It will come, Allah willing, the rest of it in the hadith, and in it: Any woman who harms her husband, neither her prayer nor any good deed of hers is accepted until she helps him and pleases him, even if she fasted perpetually, prayed at night, freed slaves, and carried arms striving in the path of Allah Almighty, she would be the first to enter the Fire if she did not please him and help him. And he said: Upon the man is the same punishment and burden if he is harmful and unjust to her. Whoever harms a woman until she ransoms herself from him, Allah Almighty will not be satisfied with any punishment for him less than the Fire, for Allah Almighty becomes angry for the woman as He becomes angry for the orphan. Any woman who seeks khul from her husband remains under the curse of Allah Almighty, the angels, His messengers, and all people. When the angel of death descends upon her, he says to her: Enter the Fire with those who enter. Verily Allah and His Messenger are free from whoever harms a woman until she seeks khul from him. Whoever is patient with the bad character of his wife, seeking reward from Allah Almighty, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will give him reward like what He gave Ayyub for his affliction, and upon her will be burden every day and night like the sand of Alij; if she dies before helping him and pleasing him, she will be raised on the Day of Resurrection inverted with the hypocrites in the lowest depth of the Fire. Whoever has a wife who does not agree with him, does not bear patiently what Allah Almighty provided, burdens him and loads him beyond his capacity, no good deed will be accepted from her; if she dies upon that, she will be raised with those who earned anger."
"1914","Chapter 21 - Forbidding the woman from delaying when her husband calls her. 1605 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Maysarah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, raising the hadith: Allah has cursed the procrastinating women? It was said: Who are the procrastinating women? It was said: The man calls the woman to his bed, and she says: Later, later, until his eyes are overcome by sleep."
"1915","1606 - With this chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman to sleep until she offers herself to her husband. He said: How does she offer herself to her husband? He said: She removes her clothes and enters with him under his blanket, pressing her skin to his skin; when she does that, she has offered herself."
"1916","1607 - Abu Yala said: Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kufi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Ala ar-Razi, from al-Ala ibn Abdurrahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the procrastinating woman and the one who falsely claims menstruation; as for the procrastinating one, she is the one who when her husband desires her says: Later now. As for the one who falsely claims, she is the one who when her husband desires her says: I am menstruating, while she is not menstruating."
"1917","1608/1 - al-Walid ibn Shuja Abu Hammam and Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas narrated to us, both saying: Baqiyyah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Zufar narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from one who heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has intercourse with his wife, let him satisfy her; if he precedes her, let him not rush her."
"1918","1608/2 - Abu Hammam narrated to us, Abdulmajid ibn Abdulaziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from one who narrated to him from Anas, with it similarly."
"1919","Chapter 22 - Coitus interruptus. 1609 - Ishaq: Abu Usamah informed us, Isa ibn Sinan Abu Sinan narrated to us, Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn as-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The first to practice withdrawal were a group of the Ansar; they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A group of the Ansar practice withdrawal, so he was alarmed and said: A soul decreed to be created will come to be, and he neither commanded nor forbade."
"1920","1610 - Ahmad ibn Mani: Abu an-Nadr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from a man of Sulaym, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said anything about it, it is as he said, meaning withdrawal. I see no harm in it; it is your crop: if you wish you leave it thirsty, and if you wish you water it."
"1921","1611 - Abu Bakr said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, from Mandal ibn Ali, from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Jarir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I only reached you safely from the polytheists with a young slave girl, and I practice withdrawal from her, intending to sell her? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is decreed will come to her."
"1922","1612 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Umarah al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Saeed, may Allah be pleased with him, that he mentioned a hadith about withdrawal and said: I practiced withdrawal from a slave girl of mine, and she gave birth to the most beloved person to me, this boy."
"1923","1613 - Musaddad said: Abdulwarith narrated to us, from Abdulaziz ibn Suhayb, from Abdulwahid al-Bunani, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and asked him about withdrawal, so he struck with his hand toward what was next to him, and the man turned away, so he pelted him and said: Uff! Abdulaziz said: I mentioned that to Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, so he said: We saw no harm in it."
"1924","1614 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and the companions of Abdullah, who said: There is no harm in withdrawal."
"1925","Chapter 23 - Approaching the woman in her anus. More of that will come, Allah willing, in the commentary of Surah al-Baqarah. Some of it preceded in treatment of women. 1615 - Al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Amr ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1926","1616 - With it: from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him. He said in the narration of Samurah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The posteriors of women are forbidden to you. And he said in the narration of Imran, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade approaching women in their backs. He added in it: al-Hasan said: Does that except every foolish wicked one?"
"1927","1617/1 - Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn Saeed ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us. 1617/1 - Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqi narrated to us, who said: Uthman ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, from Zamah ibn Salih. Ad-Dawraqi said in his narration: from Ibn Tawus. Muhammad said in his narration: from Salamah ibn Wahram. Then they agreed, from Ibn Tawus, from Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be shy before Allah Almighty, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their anuses."
"1928","Chapter 24 - Perfume for the married one. 1618 - Ishaq said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, from Imran ibn Jafar, Muhammad ibn Nudaylah narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Abdullah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said that when he married Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Make most of the dowry in perfume."
"1929","Chapter 25 - What is said to the married one. 1619 - Abu Yala said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abu Maslamah, from Abu Nadrah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Umm Salamah sent me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then he took my hand and we went out, and he had recently married Zaynab bint Jahsh, may Allah be pleased with her, so he passed by his wives who congratulated him, and the people congratulated him, saying: Praise be to Allah, may Allah delight your eye, O Messenger of Allah! the hadith."
"1930","1620/1 - Abu Bakr said: Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Sinan ibn Rabiah al-Bahili, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a daughter such and such, then she mentioned her beauty and loveliness, and I prefer you with her. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have accepted her. She kept praising her until she mentioned that she never had a headache nor complained of anything at all. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have no need of your daughter."
"1931","1620/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with this."
"1932","Chapter 27 - The scarcity of righteous women. 1621 - Abd said: Ibrahim ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad informed us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Buhayr ibn Sad narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to her: O Aisha, feed us. She said: By Allah, we have no food. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed us. She said: By Allah, we have no food. He said: Feed us. She said: By Allah, we have no food. So Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, a believing woman does not swear about something that it is not with her while it is with her. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How do you know whether she is a believer or not? The example of the believing woman among women is like the white-footed crow among crows, and the Fire was created for the foolish, and women are among the foolish, except the owner of the comb and the lamp."
"1933","Chapter 28 - Prohibition of intercourse in the middle and start of the month, command to cover during intercourse, and permissibility of seeing the private part. 1622 - Al-Harith said: Abdurrahim ibn Waqid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Amr informed us, from as-Sari ibn Khalid ibn Shaddad, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, do not have intercourse with your wife in the middle of the month, nor at the crescent of the new moon; have you not seen the insane seized by fits often in them?"
"1934","1623 - Ismail ibn Abi Ismail narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash informed us, from Abdurrahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, from Sad ibn Masud al-Kindi, who said: Uthman ibn Mazun, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not like to look at the private part of my wife, nor that she see that from me! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why is that? Allah Almighty has made you a garment for her. I see that from my wives, and they see it from me. He said: Who can be compared to you, O Messenger of Allah? Then he turned away, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibn Mazun is certainly modest and concealing."
"1935","1624/1 - Ibn Abi Shaybah said: Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Mandal narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you approaches his wife, let him cover himself, and let them not strip like the stripping of two donkeys."
"1936","1624/2 - Al-Bazzar narrated it from Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi, from Abu Ghassan. And he said: Mandal erred in it. Sharik mentioned that he and Mandal were with al-Amash, and Asim al-Ahwal narrated to them, from Abu Qilabah, with this hadith in mursal form."
"1937","Chapter 29 - Encouragement to marry a religious woman, and congratulating one who has a believing wife. 1625 - Musaddad said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata and Yahya ibn Jadah, who said: A woman is married for four: her beauty, her wealth, her lineage, and her religion; so take the religious and good-mannered one, may your hands be dusty! This is a good mursal."
"1938","1626 - Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Yahya ibn Jadah, narrating it, who said: The best benefit a Muslim gains after Islam is a wife who pleases him when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands her, and guards him in his wealth and herself when he is absent."
"1939","1627 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Mahdi, from Abu az-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say: Three break the back: inward poverty whose owner finds no enjoyment, a wife whom her husband trusts while she betrays him, and a ruler who angers Allah Almighty and pleases people. The righteousness of the believing woman is like seventy truthful women, and the wickedness of the wicked woman is like the wickedness of a thousand wicked women. Abu al-Yaman followed him, from Abu Mahdi: Saeed ibn Sinan. Al-Bazzar reported it."
"1940","1628 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hazm, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women are but playthings; whoever takes a plaything, let him treat it well, or let him consider it good."
"1941","Chapter 30 - Bringing the woman to her husband. 1629 - Ishaq said: Abdurrazzaq informed us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, and from Abu Yazid al-Madini, both saying: When Fatimah was presented to Ali, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Ali: Do not approach your wife until I come to you. She said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and called for water. He said in it whatever Allah willed him to say, then sprinkled the water on the chest and face of Ali, then called Fatimah, who stood stumbling in her garment from shyness, and he sprinkled upon her too. Then he looked and saw darkness behind the house, and said: Who is this? Asma said: It is I. He said: Asma bint Umays? She said: Yes. He said: Did you come with the daughter of the Messenger of Allah honoring the Messenger of Allah? I said: Yes, so he supplicated for me with a supplication that is the most precious of my deeds to me, and he said: O Fatimah, I spared no effort in marrying you to the most beloved of my family to me. Then he went out and said to Ali: Take your wife, then he turned to a chamber, and kept supplicating for them until he entered his chamber. I said: Its men are trustworthy, but Asma bint Umays was at this time in Abyssinia with her husband Jafar, there is no disagreement about that, so perhaps that was her sister Salma bint Umays, the wife of Hamzah ibn Abdulmuttalib."
"1942","1630 - Abu Yala said: Shayban, who is Ibn Farrukh, narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from one who narrated to him, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A woman has impressed me, who does not give birth; shall I marry her? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, and he turned away from her. Then his soul followed her, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this woman and her like impressed me, her charm and the like impressed me, shall I marry her? He said: No; a black fertile woman is more beloved to me than her. Did you not know that I will outnumber the nations by you on the Day of Resurrection, so the offspring of the Muslims will come holding their fathers by the waist, and it will be said to them: Enter Paradise, until I see the miscarried fetus stubbornly lagging, and it will be said to him: Enter Paradise! He will say: O Lord, and my parents? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: Enter you Paradise, and your parents Paradise."
"1943","1631 - Abu Yala also said: Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Siyah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the beautiful barren woman, and take the black fertile one, for I will outnumber the nations by you, until the miscarried fetus will remain stubborn at the gate of Paradise, and it will be said to him: Enter Paradise! He will say: Until my parents enter with me."
"1944","1632 - Husayn ibn Yazid at-Tahhan narrated to us, Saeed ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid, from as-Sari ibn Ismail, from ash-Shabi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of your women among the people of Paradise? The loving fertile one, who when she wrongs or is wronged says: I will not taste sleep until you are pleased."
"1945","1633 - Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Bakhtari al-Wasiti Abu Abdullah al-Makfuf narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Abdurrahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi informed us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever marries has been given double worship."
"1946","1634 - Al-Harith said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, who said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Mughallis narrated to me, who said: I heard Abu Najih as-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is able to marry and does not marry is not from me."
"1947","1635 - Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Ubayd ibn Sad, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever loves my natural disposition, let him follow my practice, and marriage is part of my practice."
"1948","1636 - Zakariyya narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hujayr, from Tawus, who said: The rites of a youth are not complete until he marries."
"1949","1637 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Zajir ibn as-Salt informed us, from al-Harith ibn Umayr, from Shaddad, from Abu Talhah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O youth of Quraysh, do not commit adultery; whoever keeps his youth safe will enter Paradise."
"1950","1638 - Abu Talib Abduljabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, from Atiyyah ibn Busr, who said: Attaf ibn Wadaah al-Hilali came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Attaf, do you have a wife? He said: No. He said: Nor a slave girl? He said: No. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And you are healthy and wealthy? He said: Yes, praise be to Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you are among the brothers of the devils; either you are of the monasticism of the Christians and you are of them, or you are of us, so do as we do, for marriage is part of our practice. The worst of you are your unmarried, and the meanest of your dead are your unmarried; Satan has no weapon against me more effective among the righteous men than women except the married; those are the purified, cleared of indecency. Woe to you, O Attaf, they are the companions of Dawud, the companions of Ayyub, the companions of Yusuf, and the companions of Kursuf, the hadith. Woe to you, O Attaf, marry, for you are among those given increase. He said: Attaf said: O Messenger of Allah, I will not marry until you marry me to whomever you wish. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have married you, in the name of Allah Almighty and His blessing, to Karimah bint Kulthum al-Himyari."
"1951","Chapter 31 - Encouragement to marry. 1639 - Ishaq said: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, Hushaym informed us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Utbah ibn Farqad offered marriage to his son and he refused, so he mentioned that to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said to him: Has the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not married, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, married, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, married, and we have of them what we have? He said: O Commander of the Believers, who has deeds like the deeds of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and like your deeds? When he said: like your deeds, he said: Stop; if you wish marry, and if you wish do not."
"1952","1640 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Saeed ibn Jubayr, who said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, said to me, and that was before my face grew hair: Have you married, O Ibn Jubayr? I said: No, and I do not intend that this day of mine. He said: What was in your loins of those entrusted will come forth. Authentic as stopped, and part of it is in the Sahih."
"1953","1641 - Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about things in which a man is rewarded, even in approaching his wife, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, how so, while it is his desire he fulfills? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you see if it were forbidden, would he not bear sin? They said: Yes. He said: Likewise he is rewarded."
"1954","1642 - Al-Harith said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from al-Hasan, who said: A group gathered and said: If only we sent to the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked them about his character (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they sent to them, and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prays, sleeps, fasts, breaks fast, and marries women. They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been forgiven his past and future sins, so some of them said: I will stand the night and not sleep, some said: I will fast the day and not break fast, and some said: I will leave women and not approach them, for in them is distraction. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) learned of that and said: What is with men who inquire into the affair of their Prophet, and when they were informed of it they turned away from it, so some said such and such? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But I sleep and stand, break fast and fast, and marry; whoever turns away from my practice is not from me."
"1955","1643 - Abu Yala said: Abu Ali ash-Shaylamani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ismail narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Salih, freedman of at-Tawamah, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any youth who marries in his early age, his devil cries out: Woe to him, woe to him; he has protected his religion from me!"
"1956","1644 - With this chain: to Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: If only one day remained of my term, I would meet Allah Almighty with a wife; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The worst of you are your unmarried. These are two objectionable hadiths, and Khalid is accused of lying."
"1957","Chapter 32 - Prohibition of travel without need for the woman. 1645 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Hanafi informed us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrami informed us, from Uthman al-Akhnasi, from Abdurrahman ibn Sad ibn Yarbu, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us in the Farewell Pilgrimage: This is the pilgrimage, then sitting upon the backs of mats in houses. Ibn Abi Saminah said: It is only Abdurrahman ibn Saeed, but thus he said."
"1958","1646 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Asim ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj with his wives, he said: It is only this one, then you must stay upon the backs of mats. The hadith of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, from the letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), preceded at the beginning of marriage."
"1959","1647 - At-Tayalisi said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Kahmas al-Hilali, who said: I was with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and while we were sitting with him, a woman came and sat with him, and said: O Commander of the Believers, my husband has much evil and little good. He said to her: Who is your husband? She said: Abu Salamah. He said: That is a man with companionship, and he is a truthful man. Then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to a man sitting with him: Is it not so? He said: O Commander of the Believers, we know him only as you said. He said to a man: Stand and call him to me. The woman stood when he sent for her husband and sat behind Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. They soon came together until he sat before Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, so Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: What does this one sitting behind me say? He said: Who is she, O Commander of the Believers? He said: This is your wife. He said: What does she say? He said: She claims your good is little and your evil much. He said: Evil is what she said, O Commander of the Believers! She is among the most righteous of her women, most clothed and most comfortable in house, but her stallion is weak. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the woman: What do you say? She said: He spoke truth. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, rose to her with the stick and struck her with it, then said: O enemy of herself, you ate his wealth and consumed his youth, then you speak of what is not in him? She said: O Commander of the Believers, do not hasten, by Allah I will never sit this sitting again! So he ordered three garments for her, saying: Take this for what I did to you, and beware of complaining about this old man. He said: As if I look at her standing with the garments, then he, may Allah be pleased with him, turned to her husband and said: Let what you saw me do to her not carry you to mistreat her. He said: I would not do it! He said: Go, then he mentioned the hadith. It will come, Allah willing, in the merit of the first generation."
"1960","1648 - Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu Hariz, from al-Hakam: A woman from Tayy of Banu Sinbis, called Umm Bal, came to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, with her husband, and said: Her husband does not approach her, and she is a woman who wants children. The man said: Do you not see what favor is upon her? He said: She was in a fine appearance. He said to him: Not even by magic where the old man is aroused? He said: Not even by magic. He said: You are ruined and have ruined. He turned to her and said to her: Be patient until he is relieved."
"1961","Chapter 34 - What is upon the woman of house service. 1649 - Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah informed us, from Damrah ibn Habib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed upon his daughter Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, service inside the house, and upon Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, what was outside the house."
"1962","1650/1 - Abu Bakr said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The women said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the merit in jihad, so do we have any of our deeds by which we reach the merit of jihad? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, the work of one of you in her house attains thereby the merit of jihad."
"1963","1650/2 - Abu Yala said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Raja Rawh ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us with it."
"1964","1650/3 - Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abu Raja informed us with it."
"1965","Chapter 35 - Guardians. 1651 - Musaddad said: Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from al-Hasan and Mughirah, from Ibrahim, who said: No marriage except with a guardian, or the ruler."
"1966","1652 - Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: No marriage except with a guardian."
"1967","1653 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, Baqiyyah informed us, Mubashshir ibn Ubayd informed us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women are not married except from equals, none marry them off except guardians, and no dowry less than ten dirhams."
"1968","Chapter 36 - Permissibility of concealing some defects of the woman that do not establish choice. 1654 - Al-Harith said: Yazid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from ash-Shabi, who said: A man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I have a daughter whom I buried alive in ignorance, then I extracted her and she became Muslim, then she incurred a prescribed punishment, then she took a blade and slaughtered herself, and I caught her having cut some of her jugular veins, so I treated her and she healed, then she became devout and devoted herself to the Quran. She is being proposed to me, and what happened of her affair prevents me. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Do you set out to uncover a cover Allah Almighty covered? If it reaches me that you mentioned anything of her affair, I will make you an example for the people of the cities; rather marry her as a chaste Muslim woman."
"1969","Book 17 - The wedding feast. 1 - Chapter on one who leaves accepting for other than the wedding feast. 1655 - Abu Yala said: Hayyan ibn Bishr Abu Abdurrahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Talhah, from al-Hasan al-Basri, who said: Uthman ibn Abi al-As was invited to a circumcision and refused to accept, so he was asked about that, and he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would not attend circumcision, nor be invited to it."
"1970","1656 - Jubarah ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghirab narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, that he was invited to food, and when he came he said: What is this? They said: The circumcision of a girl. So he stood and did not eat, saying: This is something we were not invited to in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1971","2 - Chapter on the wedding feast and its amount. 1657 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to us, that he said: It reached me from Asma bint Umays, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me sa measures of dates and barley, saying: When the women of the Ansar enter upon you, feed them from it, meaning at the wedding of Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her."
"1972","1658 - Abu Yala said: Ibrahim ibn Saeed narrated to us, Abu an-Nadr informed us, Abu Jafar ar-Razi informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the wedding feast three days."
"1973","1659 - Al-Harith said: Abdurrahim ibn Waqid narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Rashid al-Khurasani informed us, al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us, from Anbasah ibn Abdurrahman, from Muhammad ibn AbdusSamad, from Abu Ruman, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about wedding food, and it was said: O Commander of the Believers, why is wedding food more fragrant than our food? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In wedding food is a weight of the fragrance of Paradise. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Ibrahim the close friend, upon him prayer and peace, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for it to be blessed and made fragrant. This is a dark chain."
"1974","3 - Chapter on permission to leave for one who sees wrongdoing. In it is the hadith of Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, coming, Allah willing, in the Book of Clothing in the chapter forbidding covering walls. 1660 - Abu Yala said: Abu Hammam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Bakr ibn Mudar informed me, from Amr, who said: A man invited Abdullah ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, to a wedding feast, and when he came he heard amusement, so he did not enter, and he said: What is with you? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever multiplies the multitude of a people is of them, and whoever is pleased with the deed of a people is a partner of whoever did it. The hadith of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, will come, Allah willing, in the Book of Drinks."
"1975","4 - Chapter on accepting the invitation to the wedding feast. 1661 - Abu Yala said: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hababah bint Ajlan narrated to us, from her mother Umm Hafs, from Safiyyah bint Jarir, from Umm Hakim bint Wada al-Khuzaiyyah, who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is returning kindness disliked? He said: How ugly it is! If a trotter were gifted to me I would accept it, and if I were invited to it I would accept."
"1976","1662 - Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Malik informed us, from Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Yala ibn Murrah, from Iyad ibn Abi Ashras, who said: I saw Yala ibn Murrah and invited him to a feast, so he sat fasting, and people ate while he did not taste. We said to him: By Allah, had we known you were fasting we would not have troubled you! He said: Do not say that, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Accept your brother, for you are thereby upon good; either a right you witnessed, or otherwise you forbid him from it and command him to good. The mursal hadith of Mujahid is in the Shamil."
"1977","5 - Chapter on dislike of entering the wedding feast without invitation. 1663 - Abu Dawud said: al-Yaman Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Abi Uthman, from Saeed al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Whoever enters upon food without being invited to it enters as a sinner and eats unlawfully."
"1978","6 - Chapter on the right of the husband over the wife. 1664/1 - Abu Dawud said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a woman came to him and said: What is the right of the husband over his wife? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She does not withhold herself from him even if she is on the back of a saddle, nor give anything from his house except with his permission; if she does that, he has the reward and upon her is the burden. She does not fast a voluntary day except with his permission; if she does that, she sins and is not rewarded. She does not leave his house except with his permission; if she does, the angels curse her: the angels of anger and the angels of mercy, until she repents or returns. It was said: Even if he is unjust? He said: Even if he is unjust."
"1979","1664/2 - Musaddad said: Abdulwahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Layth informed us, and he mentioned it, saying after his words: even if he is unjust: She said: By the One who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, no man will ever control my affair."
"1980","1664/3 - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abdurrahim, who is Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Layth, and he mentioned like the hadith of Abdulwahid."
"1981","1664/4 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Qutbah, from Layth, and he mentioned similar to the first, but did not say: It was said: even if he is unjust, to its end."
"1982","1664/5 - Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdurrahman at-Tufawi narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: A woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned similar with the wording of Jarir without the addition at its end. This difference is from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, who is weak."
"1983","1665/1 - Musaddad said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Qays informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: A woman from Khatham came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a single woman, so inform me what is the right of the husband over his wife? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of the husband over his wife is that if he asks her for herself while she is on the back of a camel, she does not refuse him. Part of the right of the husband over his wife is that she not fast a voluntary day except with his permission; if she does, she hungers and thirsts and it is not accepted from her. Part of the right of the husband over his wife is that she not give anything from his house except with his permission; if she does, the reward is for another and the misery upon her. Part of the right of the husband over the wife is that she not leave her house except with his permission; if she does, the angels of heaven, the angels of mercy, and the angels of punishment curse her until she returns or repents."
"1984","1665/2 - Abu Yala said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us."
"1985","1665/3 - Al-Bazzar said: Muhammad ibn Abdulmalik al-Qurashi narrated to us, who said: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, in full. Al-Bazzar added at its end: She said: I will never marry."
"1986","1666 - Al-Harith said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, al-Amash informed us, from Abu Zibyan, from a man of the Ansar, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: When Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, came from Yemen, he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I saw a people prostrating to one another, shall we not prostrate to you? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to command something to prostrate to something, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands. Al-Amash said: I mentioned it to Ibrahim, who said: If a woman licked the nose of her husband afflicted with leprosy, she would not fulfill his right."
"1987","1667 - Al-Harith also said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Mujalid ibn Saeed informed us, from Amir ash-Shabi, from Fatimah bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the women and said: Peace be upon you, O ingrates for favors! She said: They said: We seek refuge in Allah from denying the favor of Allah! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is angry with her husband, she says: I never saw any good from you at all!"
"1988","1668/1 - Abu Bakr said: Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, Rabiah ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Nahar, from Abu Saeed, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man brought a daughter of his to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my daughter, and she refused to marry. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Obey your father. Each time she repeated his words back to him, she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not marry until you inform me: What is the right of the husband over his wife? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he had a wound, or his nostrils flowed with blood and pus, then you licked it with your tongue, you would not fulfill his right. She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not marry them off except with their permission. 1668/2 - Al-Bazzar reported it from the hadith of Jafar, saying: We know it only by this chain, and only Jafar narrated it from Rabiah. Ibn Hibban and al-Hakim authenticated it."
"1989","1669/1 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Yahya ibn Abdulhamid narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah informed us, Thabit informed us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A woman was under a man, and her father fell ill, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is ill, and my husband refuses to permit me to nurse him! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Obey your husband. Then her father died, and she sought her husband's permission to pray over him, but her husband refused to permit her to pray, so she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to her: Obey your husband. So she obeyed her husband and did not pray over her father, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forgiven your father due to your obedience to your husband."
"1990","1669/2 - Al-Harith said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, and he mentioned it, but said: A man went to battle while his wife was upstairs and her father downstairs, and he commanded her not to leave her house, then her father fell ill, then he mentioned the hadith in full."
"1991","1670 - Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri narrated to us, from al-Ifriqi, Umarah ibn Ghurab narrated to me, who said: An aunt of his narrated to him that she asked Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, Mother of the Believers: The husband of one of us desires her and she withholds herself, either angry or not eager for him; is there any sin upon her in that? She said: Yes. His right upon you is that if he wanted you while you are on a saddle, you would not refuse him, the hadith."
"1992","1671 - Ishaq said in his Musnad: Abdurrazzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abdulkarim al-Jazari, from Ikrimah: Asma bint Abi Bakr came to her father complaining about az-Zubayr, so he said to her: Return, my daughter; if you are patient and keep good company with him, then he dies and you do not marry after him, and you both enter Paradise, you will be his wife."
"1993","1672 - Abu Yala said: Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather Abu Sallam, from Malik as-Saksaki, who is Ibn Yukhamir, who said: Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman to take from her husband's house except with her husband's permission, nor is it lawful for her to take it while he dislikes it, nor to go out while he dislikes it without his permission, nor to let anyone covet him while they are together, nor to harden his heart, nor to abandon his bed. She must not harm him, even if he is more unjust than her, but come to him until she pleases him; if he accepts from her, then well and good, Allah accepts her excuse, her proof succeeds, and there is no sin upon her. If the husband refuses to be pleased, she has conveyed her excuse to him. If she does nothing of that, but accepts estrangement until three nights pass for her. If she permits without his permission, or visits a parent or other without his permission when she witnessed with him, breaking his oath, obeying in it a parent or child, abandoning for him a bed, or hardening for him a heart, then three major sins continue to be written against them while they do that: the greatest of major sins: associating with Allah, killing a believer deliberately, and the third: consuming usury. It suffices a woman in sin that whenever her husband is angry with her, three major sins come, Satan overcomes her, and she becomes of the people of the Fire. He said: Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, also narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels continue to curse her, and Allah Almighty curses her, and the keepers of the abode of mercy and the abode of punishment, for what she violated of disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. This is a hadith whose men are trustworthy and firm except the shaykh of Abu Yala, who is of his objectionable narrations; he was truthful in himself, except that his copyist inserted into his narration what is not of his hadith, and they used to warn him of that but he would not accept. Al-Hakim reported it from another face, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Malik ibn Yukhamir as-Saksaki; the difference between the two wordings should be examined."
"1994","1673 - Ishaq said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from a man of the Ansar, from Umm Salma bint Qays, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took our pledge among women of the Ansar, taking upon us: That you not deceive your husbands. She said: When we left, we said: Did we ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is deceiving our husbands? So we returned to him and she asked him, and he said: That you betray and gift his wealth to another."
"1995","7 - Chapter on recommendation concerning women. It preceded in Hajj a hadith. 1674/1 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Zayd ibn Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, who said: Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and he mentioned a long sermon, and in it: O people, women are captives with you; you took them by the trust of Allah, and you made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah. You have a right over them, and they have a right over you. Part of your right is that they not let others tread your beds, nor disobey you in what is right; if they do that, then they have their provision and clothing in a customary manner; when you strike, strike without severity, the hadith."
"1996","1674/2 - Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from Humayd ibn Nafi, from Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade striking women, so they complained. Then he permitted them to strike them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy women surrounded the family of Muhammad tonight, all of them struck. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not like to see a man enraged, the vein of his neck upon his throat, killing her. I said: This is mursal; Umm Kulthum was born after the death of Abu Bakr."
"1997","1675 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then said: Allah Almighty enjoins you to treat women well! Allah enjoins you to treat women well! Allah enjoins you to treat women well! Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers, your fathers, your brothers, your paternal aunts, and your maternal aunts. A man of the two Scriptures marries a woman not knowing what good he has in her, and neither of them turns away from his companion until they die in old age. Abu Salamah said: I narrated this hadith to al-Ala ibn Sufyan al-Ghassani, who said: It reached me that of the indecencies Allah Almighty forbade inwardly, whose mention is not clear in the Quran, is that a man marries a woman, and when her companionship lasts, her time lengthens, and she empties what is in her womb, he divorces her without suspicion. Ibn Majah narrated from it: Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers, from another face from al-Miqdam."
"1998","1676 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hilal narrated to us, a trustworthy companion of ours informed us, from Saeed, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, upon him peace, kept enjoining me concerning women until I thought he would forbid divorcing them."
"1999","8 - Chapter on permissibility of keeping a beautiful wife for one who loves her even if there is suspicion in her. 1677 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Furat ibn Salman narrated to us, from Abdulkarim ibn Malik, from Ibn az-Zubayr or Abu az-Zubayr, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife does not repel the hand of one who touches? He said: Divorce her. He said: She is a beautiful woman, and I love her. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enjoy her."
"2000","9 - Chapter on beating the tambourine in marriage and publicizing it. 1678 - Musaddad said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Umar, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when he heard a sound would be alarmed, but if it was said: circumcision or wedding, he remained silent."
"2001","1679 - Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, who said: Muhammad ibn Sirin used to like beating the tambourine at the marriage contract."
"2002","1680/1 - At-Tayalisi said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali, who said: I witnessed Thabit ibn Wadiah and Qarazah ibn Kab al-Ansari at a wedding, and there was singing, so they were spoken to about that, and they said: Singing at weddings and weeping over the dead without wailing have been permitted."
"2003","Ahmad ibn Mani 1680/2: Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, from his father, from Amir ibn Sad, who said: I entered upon Uqbah ibn Amr, Thabit ibn Yazid, and Qarazah ibn Kab, with singing girls and basil with them. I said: Do you do this?! They said: Singing at weddings and weeping over the dead without wailing have been permitted for us."
"2004","1680/3 - He said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amir ibn Sad, who said: I entered upon Ibn Masud, Qarazah ibn Kab, and Yazid ibn Thabit, thus he said, then he mentioned it. What is preserved: Thabit ibn Yazid, who is Ibn Yazid ibn Wadiah. An-Nasai reported it through Sharik, from Abu Ishaq, mentioning: Abu Masud Uqbah ibn Amr and Qarazah ibn Kab only."
"2005","1681 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Wasi ibn Habban, from Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like publicizing marriage. Abu Abdullah, meaning Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi, said: Meaning announcing it."
"2006","10 - Chapter on what is permitted of amusement. 1682 - Al-Harith said: Abu Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Ishaq, from ash-Shabi, raising it: He passed by the players with spears and said: Take, O Banu Arfidah, so that the Jews and Christians know there is latitude in our religion. He said: While they were thus, Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, came, and when they saw him they scattered."
"2007","11 - Chapter on custody. 1683 - Ishaq said: Abu Dawud al-Hafari Umar ibn Sad informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah ar-Rabadhi, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, who said: A Bedouin man married a daughter of his uncle, and she bore him a girl, then he died leaving her, and a man of the Ansar married her after him. Her guardians said: We will not leave our daughter with them. They disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the mother said: I am the bearer, the custodian, and the nursing mother, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Whom do you choose? She said: I choose Allah and His Messenger, the abode of faith, and the Emigrants and Helpers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They shall not take her while my eye watches over her, and if I live I will place her in a position that delights her eye. He said: They disputed to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said to her: Whom do you choose? She said the same as the first saying, so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, judged her for the guardians, then Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: O Abu Bakr, so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, judged with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged her. This is a weak and also interrupted chain."
"2008","1684 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, Amir narrated to us, from Masruq, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, divorced Umm Asim, then she died, and Asim remained in the care of his grandmother, so she disputed with him to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who judged that the child be with his grandmother, and maintenance upon Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: She is more entitled to him."
"2009","1685 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Abdulaziz ibn Muhammad ad-Darawardi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Nafi ibn Ujayr, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Zayd ibn Harithah, may Allah be pleased with him, went to Makkah, and the daughter of Hamzah ibn Abdulmuttalib, may Allah be pleased with them, arrived. Jafar ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I will take her, and I am most entitled to her, the daughter of my uncle, and with me is her maternal aunt, and the maternal aunt is a mother, and she is most entitled. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Rather I am most entitled to her, she is the daughter of my uncle, and with me is the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she is most entitled to her. I raise my voice so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hears my argument before he comes out. Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Rather I am most entitled to her, I went out to her, traveled, and brought her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and said: What is your affair? Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The daughter of my uncle, and I am most entitled to her, and with me is the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), being with her is most entitled to her than others. Jafar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I am most entitled to her, O Messenger of Allah, the daughter of my uncle, and with me is her maternal aunt, and the maternal aunt is a mother, and she is most entitled to her than others. Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Rather I am most entitled to her, I went out to her, undertook the journey, and spent, so I am most entitled to her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will judge between you in this and in other. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: and in other, I said: The Quran came down about raising our voices. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, O Zayd, you are my freedman and theirs. He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, O Jafar, you resemble my creation and character, and you are of my tree from which I was created. He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, O Ali, you are my elite and trustworthy. Yazid ibn al-Had said: I mentioned that to Abdullah ibn Hasan, who said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are from me and I am from you. He, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I am pleased, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the girl, I have judged her for Jafar, to be with her maternal aunt, and the maternal aunt is a mother. They said: We submit, O Messenger of Allah."
"2010","12 - Chapter on descriptions of women. 1686 - Abu Bakr said: I was told from Abdullah ibn Idris, from Mutrah, who is Ibn Yazid, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the righteous woman among women is like the white-footed crow. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the white-footed crow? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one whose one leg is white."
"2011","13 - Chapter on the waiting period. 1687 - Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ubayd ibn Amr, who said: The woman is trusted concerning her private part."
"2012","1688/1 - Ishaq said: al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us. 1688/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Idris informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her: Move to Umm Sharik, and do not deprive us of yourself."
"2013","14 - Chapter on the residence of the woman divorced by three divorces. 1689/1 - Ishaq: Abdurrazzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: I asked Saeed ibn al-Musayyab about the thrice-divorced woman, where does she wait? He said: In the house of her husband. I said to him: Where is the hadith of Fatimah bint Qays? He said: That is a woman who caused people trial; she was sharp-tongued. Or he said: She was a woman with evil in her tongue toward her in-laws."
"2014","1689/2 - Abdurrazzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Maymun ibn Mihran informed me, who said: I discussed with Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, and he mentioned similar to the first."
"2015","1689/3 - Waki informed us, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: I came to Madinah and asked about its most knowledgeable, and I was directed to Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, so I asked him about the thrice-divorced woman, where does she wait? He said: In the house of her husband. I said: Fatimah bint Qays, sister of ad-Dahhak ibn Qays, was divorced thrice by her husband and waited in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum. He said: That is a sharp-tongued woman."
"2016","15 - Chapter on exception in divorce. 1690 - Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Mughirah, who said: I came to Ibrahim an-Nakhai and said: A man disputed with me, called Saeed, then he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then Ibrahim said: That came to me once, claiming he said to his wife: Every woman of his is divorced thrice except you. I said: Shurayh used to say: If he begins with divorce, it falls upon her. It reached me that when he went out he said: Is this except the opinion of men? Then it reached me that he was cautious about her and left her. Jarir said: I met Saeed az-Zubaydi and asked him about this, and he said: I asked Saeed ibn Jubayr, who said: She is not divorced. Then az-Zubaydi said: Were I that day in the state I am in today, I would not have divorced her."
"2017","1691/1 - Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Malik al-Lakhmi, from Makhul, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muadh, Allah has not created anything on the face of the earth more beloved to Him than emancipation, nor created anything on the face of the earth more hateful to Him than divorce. If a man says to his slave: You are free if Allah wills, he is free, and he has no exception. If he says to his wife: You are divorced if Allah wills, he has his exception, and there is no divorce in it. This is interrupted."
"2018","1691/2 - Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us with it."
"2019","16 - Chapter on the divorce of the intoxicated. 1692 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from az-Zuhri, from Aban ibn Uthman, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The divorce of the intoxicated is not valid."
"2020","17 - Chapter on the one who makes lawful. 1693 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abdullah ibn Sharik narrated to me, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, say about a man who marries a woman to make her lawful: They are two adulterers, even if they remain ten or twenty years, when he married her for that."
"2021","18 - Chapter on forbidding playing with divorce and urging divorce according to the Sunnah for one who wants it. 1694/1 - Abu Bakr said: Abdussalam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ad-Dalani, from Abu al-Ala, from Humayd ibn Abdurrahman al-Himyari, who said: It reached Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was angry with them, so he came to him and mentioned that, and he said: One of you says: I married, I divorced, but such is not the waiting period of the Muslims; divorce the woman at the start of her waiting period."
"2022","1694/2 - At-Tayalisi said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man used to say: I divorced you, I took you back. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is with men playing with the limits of Allah Almighty!"
"2023","1695 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yazid narrated to us, Hisham, who is Ibn Hassan, informed us, from Muhammad, who is Ibn Sirin, from Abidah, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man who divorces according to the Sunnah never regrets. This chain is authentic."
"2024","19 - Chapter on intention in divorce. 1696 - Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Shumayr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man proposed to a woman, and they said: We will not marry you until you divorce thrice. He said: Bear witness that I divorced thrice. When he entered upon the woman, they claimed divorce, so he said to them: How did I say? They said: We said: We will not marry you until you divorce thrice, and you divorced thrice. He said: Do you not know that I married so-and-so daughter of so-and-so and divorced her, and so-and-so was under me and I divorced her, until he counted three. They said: This is not what we meant. Shaqiq ibn Thawr came to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, and they ordered him to ask Uthman about that; when he arrived he asked him, informing that he asked Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: He has his intention."
"2025","20 - Chapter on indirect expressions of divorce. 1697 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abu Husayn narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Waththab, who said: I heard Masruq say: I heard Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, say: When he says: Your affair is in your hand, set right your affair, and I have directed you to your family if they accept it, it is one irrevocable divorce."
"2026","1698 - Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, Saeed ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to me, from his uncle Kharijah ibn Zayd, who said: Ibn Abi Atiq came to Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, weeping. He said: What makes you weep? He said: I gave my wife control of her affair and she separated from me. He said: What carried you to that? He said: Fate. He said: It is one; if you wish take her back, and if you wish leave her."
"2027","1699 - Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, about the forbidden: If he intended divorce, it is divorce, and if he did not intend divorce, it is an oath expiated."
"2028","1700 - Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Thumamah and a woman of our family narrated to me, that Kinanah ibn Thawr had a wife who bore him children in ignorance, and he said to her: What is above your waistband is forbidden. She disputed him to al-Ashari, who said: What did you intend? He said: Divorce. He said: Then it has separated her from you."
"2029","21 - Chapter on effecting three divorces in one wording when intended. 1701 - Ishaq said: Abdulala informed us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Alqamah, who said: We were with Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, and a man came to him and said: A man said to his wife: She is divorced eight times? He said: Did you say it at once? He said: Yes. He said: Do you want your wife to be separated from you? He said: Yes. He said: It is as you said. Then another came and said: A man said to his wife: Tonight she is divorced as many as the stars? He said: Did you say it at once? He said: Yes. He said: Do you want your wife to be separated from you? He said: Yes. Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned the women of the people of the earth thereupon with something I do not remember, then said: Allah has made clear to you how divorce is; whoever divorces as Allah Almighty commanded him, it is made clear to him, and whoever is confused by it, we make his confusion upon him; by Allah, do not confuse yourselves and we bear it, it is as you say. This is a stopped chain, authentic if Muhammad ibn Sirin heard it from Alqamah, and explicit declaration of his narrating this hadith occurs in the narration of al-Bayhaqi."
"2030","1702 - Ishaq said: Abdurrazzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Abbas, who said: One not consummated with, when the three are combined upon her, they fall. He said: I mentioned that to Tawus, who said: I bear witness that I heard Ibn Abbas make it one. He said: Amr said: One, even if he combined them."
"2031","1703 - With the preceding chain to Ibn Jurayj: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed me, from Burd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu Iyad, from Ibn Abbas, who said: ""The woman with whom marriage has not been consummated and the one with whom it has been consummated are the same with regard to the three (divorces)."""
"2032","1704 - Abdullah ibn Idris informed us, he said: I heard Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid narrating, from Dawud ibn Ibrahim ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: A man among my forefathers divorced his wife a thousand times, so his sons came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""Your father did not fear Allah so that Allah would make a way out for him; she is separated from him by three, and the rest is transgression; he has taken the signs of Allah in mockery."""
"2033","Chapter 22: Enforcing divorce pronounced in jest. 1705 - Al-Harith said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah reported, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jest is not allowed in three matters: divorce, marriage, and emancipation. Whoever utters them, they become binding."""
"2034","1706 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man would divorce his wife and say, ""I was joking,"" and free his slave and say, ""I was joking,"" and marry off his daughter and say, ""I was joking."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things, whoever says them in jest become binding upon him: divorce, emancipation, and marriage."" Then Allah Almighty revealed concerning that: ""And do not take the signs of Allah in mockery."""
"2035","Chapter 23: A woman divorced three times does not return until she is married (by another) and tastes the sweetness. 1707 - Abu Yala said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym reported, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ubaydullah or al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: Al-Ghumaysa or al-Rumaysa came complaining about her husband, saying he does not approach her. He said: She lies, O Messenger of Allah! I do approach her, but she wants to return to her first husband. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""She is not lawful to him until she tastes his little honey."""
"2036","1708 - Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya reported, from Yahya ibn Said, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), the same as the hadith before it: ""She is not lawful to him until she tastes the little honey."""
"2037","1709 - Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah reported, Abu Abd al-Malik al-Makki reported, Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah reported: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The 'little honey' means intercourse."""
"2038","1710 - Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Marwan reported the same, with the addition: from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He meant by the 'little honey' intercourse in marriage."""
"2039","Chapter 24: There is no divorce before marriage. 1711 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj reported, he said: It was narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""There is no divorce before marriage."""
"2040","1712/1 - Ibn Jurayj said: And Amr ibn Shuayb said, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the same."
"2041","1713 - Waki narrated to us, Sufyan reported, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from one who heard Tawus saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no divorce before marriage."""
"2042","1714/1 - Abu Bakr said: Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Ata and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), raising it (to the Prophet): There is no divorce before marriage, and no emancipation before ownership."
"2043","1714/2 - Al-Bazzar said: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd reported, from Ibn Abi Dhib with the same. And al-Bazzar said: It is narrated from Ibn Abi Dhib, from one who narrated to him, from Muhammad and Ata."
"2044","1714/3 - Al-Harith said: Ismail ibn Abi Ismail narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash reported, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no divorce before marriage..."" the hadith."
"2045","1714/4 - Al-Tayalisi said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, one who heard Ata narrated to me, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no divorce if he has not married, and no emancipation if he does not own."""
"2046","1714/5 - Al-Yaman Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), the same as the hadith of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"2047","1714/6 - Kharijah ibn Musab narrated to us, Haram ibn Uthman reported, from Abu Atiq with the same."
"2048","1712/2 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib reported, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Tawus, from Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""There is no divorce for one who has not married, no emancipation for one who does not own, and no vow involving disobedience to Allah Almighty."""
"2049","Chapter 25: The dislike of divorce. 1715 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray reported, Bishr ibn Numayr reported, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him): A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking permission about marrying, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I have married three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Marry, but do not divorce, for Allah Almighty hates the men who taste (many wives) and the women who taste (many husbands)."""
"2050","Chapter 26: The number of divorces. 1716 - Al-Harith said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Khalid reported, from Ismail ibn Sumay, from Abu Razin, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I heard Allah Almighty say, ""Divorce is twice,"" so where is the third? He said: ""Then either retention in kindness or release with kindness."""
"2051","Chapter 27: Rebuke for claiming descent from other than one's fathers. 1717 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Uyaynah reported, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: O Messenger of Allah, who am I? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You are Sad ibn Malik ibn Wahb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah; whoever says other than that, upon him is the curse of Allah Almighty."""
"2052","Chapter 28: A woman belongs to the last of her husbands in the Hereafter. 1718 - Abu Yala said: Ismail ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abu al-Malih reported, from Maymun ibn Mihran, who said: Muawiyah proposed to Umm al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with them both), but she refused to marry him. She said: I heard Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The woman belongs to the last of her husbands,"" and I do not want a replacement for Abu al-Darda."
"2053","Chapter 29: Physiognomy (al-qafah). 1719/1 - Ishaq said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid heard his father saying: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent for a man from Banu Zuhrah while he was in the Hijr. He said: So I went with him to him, and he had lived through the pre-Islamic age, and he asked him about children of the pre-Islamic age. Sufyan said: The people of the pre-Islamic age had no waiting period for their women; when a man died the woman left and remarried without observing a waiting period. He said: So he asked him about the semen, and he said: As for the semen it is from so-and-so, but the child is attributed to the bed of so-and-so. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""He spoke the truth, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled that the child belongs to the bed."" When the man turned away he said: Tell us about the building of the Kabah. He said: Quraysh gathered strength to build the Kabah and borrowed. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He spoke the truth. I said: Ahmad and Ibn Majah narrated only the raised (marfu) part of it. 1719/2 - And Ibn Abi Umar narrated it in his Musnad like the narration of Ishaq in full. He also narrated from the hadith of Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), something of it."
"2054","1720 - Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah reported, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq saying: Nasr ibn al-Hajjaj claimed Abdullah ibn Rabah, the freedman of Khalid ibn al-Walid; Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn al-Walid stood and said: My freedman, born on my father's bed. Nasr said: My brother; he and my daughters are of the same standing. He said: Their dispute lengthened, so they entered upon Muawiyah with Fihr under his head, and both claimed him. Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone."" Nasr said: Then where is this judgment of yours, O Muawiyah, regarding Ziyad? Muawiyah said: The judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is better than the judgment of Muawiyah. He said: Abdullah ibn Rabah would not respond to Nasr regarding what he claimed, so Nasr said: Thari."
"2055","Chapter 30: Temporary marriage (mutah). 1721 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), while I stood at his head, saying, when a man said to him: Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade mutah. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""Look; if it is in the Book of Allah Almighty then he has lied against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if it is not in the Book of Allah Almighty then it is as he said."" This is an authentic hadith, halted (at a Companion); by his saying ""in the Book of Allah Almighty"" he meant His Almighty saying, ""So whatever you enjoy from them..."" the verse. And Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) argued by it, as occurs in al-Bukhari from him."
"2056","1722 - Al-Harith said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar reported, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: When Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) was asked about mutah, she would say: ""Between me and you is the Book of Allah Almighty."" Allah Almighty said: ""And those who guard their private parts, except from their wives..."" the verse. She said: ""Whoever seeks other than what Allah Almighty has joined to him in marriage or what he owns has transgressed."""
"2057","1723 - Bishr ibn Umar narrated to me, Ikrimah ibn Ammar reported, Abdullah ibn Said narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Marriage, divorce, and inheritance have demolished mutah."" Thus said Bishr ibn Umar."
"2058","1724 - Abu Yala said: Abu Musa narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail reported, Ikrimah ibn Ammar reported, Said informed me, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were in the expedition of Tabuk, and we stopped at Thaniyyat al-Wada. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lamps and women weeping, and said: ""What is this?"" It was said: Women with whom mutah was contracted, and they are weeping. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is forbidden."" Or he said: ""Marriage, divorce, the waiting period, and inheritance have demolished mutah."""
"2059","1725 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Nafi narrating, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Had I acted earlier concerning mutah with women, I would have stoned."""
"2060","Chapter 31: Requiring a waiting period (istibra) and encouragement regarding slave-girls. 1726 - Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar reported, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: ""If he buys her as a virgin, he may if he wishes not require her to observe istibra."" Ayyub said: He meant that concerning a captive woman."
"2061","1727/1 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, al-Qasim and Makhul reported, from Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar that pregnant women be approached in intercourse until they give birth."
"2062","1727/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Mamar al-Hudhali Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Usamah reported... and he mentioned it at length."
"2063","1728 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Bishr - he is Ibn al-Sari - narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Said al-Hashimi reported, a cousin of mine from Banu Hashim narrated to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Keep to concubines, for they are blessed in the wombs."" This is mursal with no harm in its chain. It has been narrated connected from the hadith of Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him); al-Hakim brought it, and its chain is very feeble, so that Ibn al-Jawzi brought it in his Fabrications."
"2064","1729 - Abu Yala said: Zahmawaih narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad reported, from Yahya ibn Said: A trustworthy man informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar that pregnant women be approached in intercourse, saying: ""Would you water another man's crop?!""."
"2065","1730 - Al-Tayalisi said: Rabah ibn Abi Maruf narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that pregnant captive women be approached in intercourse."
"2066","1731 - Al-Harith said: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Humayd ibn al-Aswad and Yazid ibn Ibrahim reported, from Humayd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) required Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) to observe istibra. It was said to him: Is she of the Mothers of the Believers or of the mothers of children? He said: ""Of the Mothers of the Believers."""
"2067","Chapter 32: Travel of a woman in her waiting period. 1732 - Musaddad said: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla reported, from Ata, who said: ""Aishah took Umm Kulthum, her sister, the wife of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah (may Allah be pleased with them), under her care, and performed Hajj with her during her waiting period."""
"2068","Chapter 33: The waiting period ends with delivery. 1733 - Ishaq said: Sufyan informed us, from Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran, from his father, who said: Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah was married to al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam. He went out to prayer while labor seized her, and she concealed it from him. She said to him: Gladden my heart with a divorce. So he divorced her, and returned after she had given birth. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he said: ""The decree has reached its term; propose to her for herself."" He said: She deceived me; may Allah Almighty deceive her!"
"2069","Chapter 34: Combining two sisters through right-hand possession, and a woman and her daughter through right-hand possession. 1734/1 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Awn, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, who said: Ibn al-Kawwa asked Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about two sister slave-girls, and he said: ""One verse permitted them and one verse forbade them; I do not do it myself, nor anyone of my household, and I neither permit it nor forbid it."""
"2070","1734/2 - Abu Yala said: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah reported, from Abu Awn, he said: I heard Abu Salih saying: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Ask me, for you do not ask one like me, and you will not ask one like me."" Ibn al-Kawwa said: Tell us about two owned sisters, and about a brother's daughter through nursing? He said: Ask about what concerns you, for you are going into bewilderment. He said: I only ask you about what we do not know; as for what we know, we do not ask about it. He said: ""As for the two owned sisters, one verse permitted them and one verse forbade them; I neither command it nor forbid it, and neither I nor my household do it."""
"2071","1735 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Malik: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, who said: Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about two sister slave-girls from right-hand possession, and he said: ""One verse permitted them and one verse forbade them, and I do not like to do it."" That reached a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Had I charge of any of the Muslims' affairs and such a one were brought to me, I would make him an example. Al-Zuhri said: I think it was Ali (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2072","1736 - And with the same chain, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from his father, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a woman and her daughter from right-hand possession, and he said: ""I do not like to permit them both together, and I forbid them both together."""
"2073","1737 - Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating that Muadh ibn Ubaydullah ibn Mamar asked Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), saying: I have a slave-girl I have touched, and she has a grown daughter; may I touch her? She forbade him that. He said: No, unless you say: It is forbidden. She said: ""None of my family does it, nor anyone who obeys me."""
"2074","1738 - Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked about it and forbade it."
"2075","Chapter 35: On invocation of curses (lian) and on jealousy. 1739 - Ishaq said: Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Abu Mashar reported, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Said ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Sad ibn Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to him and said: If I find a man upon my wife's belly shall I strike him with the sword? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What proof is clearer than the sword?"" Then he retracted his saying and said: ""The Book of Allah Almighty, and a witness."" Sad ibn Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: What proof is clearer than the sword? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Book of Allah Almighty, and a witness."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O company of the Ansar, this is Sad, whom jealousy has provoked until he opposed the Book of Allah Almighty!"" A man of the Ansar said: Sad is jealous; he never married a previously married woman, and none of us could marry a woman he divorced. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Sad is jealous, and I am jealous, and Allah is more jealous than me."" An Ansari man said: What does Allah Almighty feel jealousy over? He said: ""Over a man striving in the path of Allah Almighty whose family is betrayed in his absence."" It has a break in it as I think, and Abu Mashar is weak."
"2076","1740 - Abu Yala said: Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthmah - he is Ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah, named after his grandfather - reported, Musa ibn Yaqub - he is al-Zamai - narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb, who said: His father informed him, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter upon his wives every morning and greet them. One of them had honey with her, and when he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her she would bring him some of it, so he would stay with her. Aishah and Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with them both) were troubled by that, and when he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon them they said: O Messenger of Allah, we smell maghafir from you! So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left that honey."
"2077","1741 - Ishaq said: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Habib ibn al-Shahid reported, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi - he is the father of Adi ibn Abi Adi - from Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: O Zayd ibn Thabit, do you not know that we used to recite among what we recited: ""Do not disown your fathers, for that is disbelief in you""? He said: Yes."
"2078","1742 - Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj reported, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the matter of the two who invoked curses occurred before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I would not like to be the first of the four."""
"2079","1743 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman reported, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Jafar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked curses between al-Ajlani and his wife - he is Uwaymir ibn al-Harith - invoking curses between them over a pregnancy."""
"2080","Chapter 36: Marrying women of the People of the Book. 1744/1 - Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam reported, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, who said: Kab ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) wanted to marry a Jewish woman, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who forbade him, saying: ""She will not make you chaste."""
"2081","1744/2 - Abu Bakr said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us with the same."
"2082","Chapter 37: Giving choice to one who accepts Islam with more than four wives among them. 1745 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Zuhri - he is al-Makhzumi - reported, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sufyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: ""Ghaylan accepted Islam with ten wives under him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to choose four of them and part from the rest. And Safwan (may Allah be pleased with him) accepted Islam with eight wives, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to keep four of them and part from the rest."""
"2083","Chapter 38: Ila (vow of abstention from wives). 1746 - Musaddad said: Al-Harith ibn Ubayd Abu Qudamah narrated to us, Amir al-Ahwal reported, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: ""The ila of the pre-Islamic age was a year, two years, and more than that. Then Allah Almighty fixed four months for them; whoever's ila is less than four months is not ila."" Ata said: And if he takes the vow from her while she is in her family's house before she is brought to him, it is not ila."
"2084","Chapter 39: Zihar. 1747 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, from Said ibn Amr ibn Sulaym, who said: I asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad about a man who says: If I marry so-and-so she is divorced? He said: A man came to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: I said: If I marry so-and-so she is zihar (like my mother's back). He said: ""If you marry her and wish to keep her, expiate."""
"2085","1748 - Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan: Yaqub al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, who said: A man made zihar from his wife until Ramadan ends - or he said: made zihar from her for Ramadan - then he approached his wife at night... and he mentioned the hadith at length as mursal."
"2086","1749 - Al-Harith said: Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wahb reported, Ayyub reported, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, who said: A woman of Banu Bayadah sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wasq of barley - or he said: half a wasq of barley; Ayyub doubted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to the one who had made zihar from his wife and said: ""Give this in charity, for every half-sa of wheat is compensated by a sa of barley in its place."""
"2087","1750 - Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Numayr informed us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that a man made zihar from his wife, then saw her in the moonlight and was taken by her, so he fell upon her. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. He said: ""Has not Allah Almighty said: before they touch one another?"" He said: I saw her and she pleased me! He said: ""Refrain until you expiate."""
"2088","Chapter 40: Nursing. 1751 - Al-Harith said: Umar ibn Salih narrated to us, from Nafi, from Salih, freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What removes from me the blame of nursing? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The ghurrah,"" meaning a slave or slave-girl."
"2089","1752 - Musaddad said: Yahya reported, from Humayd al-Tawil, from al-Hasan, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Would you marry the daughter of Hamzah (may Allah be pleased with him)? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""She is the daughter of my brother through nursing, and nursing forbids what lineage forbids."""
"2090","1753/1 - Al-Tayalisi said: Kharijah ibn Musab narrated to us, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no nursing after weaning, and no orphanhood after puberty..."" the hadith."
"2091","1753/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, Makhlad reported, from Ibn Jurayj, from Mutarrif, from Haram ibn Uthman with the same."
"2092","1754 - Ibn Abi Umar said: Bishr - he is Ibn al-Sari - narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ismail al-Qurashi al-Sahmi reported, from his brother Zayd or Ziyad ibn Ismail, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade seeking nursing from a foolish woman, saying: ""Milk imparts likeness."""
"2093","1755 - Marwan narrated to us, from Ismail, he said: I heard Qays saying: al-Mughirah ibn Shubah said: ""A single nursing (al-ayfah) does not forbid."" We said: What is al-ayfah? He said: A woman gives birth and her milk is confined in her breast, so her slave-girl nurses from her once or twice."
"2094","1756 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf reported, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Seek nursing among Muzaynah, for they are trustworthy people."""
"2095","Chapter 41: Maintenance. The story of Asim ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) on custody has preceded. 1757/1 - Ishaq said: Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Abu Ibrahim al-Madani - he is Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd - reported, Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri narrated to me, from his father, who said: Amr ibn Umayyah went out to the market, and while he was bargaining over a cloak Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) appeared before him and said: What is this, O Amr? He said: I want to buy it, then give it in charity! He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You are then you. Umar paid, and Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) bought it; he entered upon his wife and said: I have given it to you in charity. Then he went out to the market and sat in his place. Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) met him and said: What became of the cloak? He told him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whatever you give them (your wives) of anything is charity for you."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: So he called from the door: O mother, and she said: To you, O Amr, what is wrong? He said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Do not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! He said: So I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whatever you give them of anything is charity for you""? She said: O Allah, yes."
"2096","1757/2 - Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd reported, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, who said: Amr ibn Umayyah went out to the market and bargained over a cloak... and he mentioned it the same. And he said: So I came to Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), and Amr said: O mother."
"2097","1757/3 - Abdullah ibn Shirawayh, narrator of Ishaq's Musnad from him, said: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Aswad reported, Humayd ibn Abi al-Aswad reported, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that he went out to the market bargaining over a cloak... and he mentioned the hadith similarly, mentioning Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) in the hadith. I said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd is weak, and his saying ""from his grandfather"" in this last chain is meaningless. The hadith from Amr ibn Umayyah has been brought by Ahmad."
"2098","1757/4 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Hammam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said... and he mentioned it. The story was not mentioned, nor the hadith of Aishah (may Allah be pleased with them both). Umayyah has no Companionship, as I explained in my book on the Companions. 1757/5 - Al-Tayalisi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd as Abu Amir and al-Nadr said. Al-Nasai narrated it in al-Kubra through another way, from the narration of al-Zibriqan ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, from Amr with it."
"2099","1757/6 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Hatim reported, Yaqub ibn Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umayyah reported, from his father, from Amr ibn Umayyah, who said: Uthman ibn Affan or Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with them both) was brought a cloak and deemed it costly, so it was passed to Amr ibn Umayyah, who bought it and clothed his wife Sukhaylah bint Ubaydah ibn al-Harith with it. Uthman or Abd al-Rahman (may Allah be pleased with them both) passed by him and said: What became of the cloak? Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I gave it in charity to Sukhaylah bint Ubaydah. He said: ""Is all that you do for your family charity?"" Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that. What Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) said was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Amr spoke the truth; all that you do for your family is charity."""
"2100","1758/1 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Umar ibn Said al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi reported, from Makhul, from Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: She heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advising one of his family, saying: ""Spend upon your family from your means, do not lift your stick from them, and make them fear Allah Almighty."" The hadith."
"2101","1758/2 - Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz reported with the same."
"2102","1758/3 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said reported, from al-Zuhri, who said: The one advised with this advice is Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2103","1759 - Al-Tayalisi said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever has two daughters, or two sisters, or female relatives, and spends upon them until he suffices them or Allah Almighty enriches them from His bounty - they will be a veil for him from the Fire."""
"2104","1760 - Al-Harith said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq reported, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Muslim ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and a youth asked his permission to go out with it. He said: ""Have you left anyone capable among your family?"" He said: I know none; they are small children. He said: ""Return to them, for among them is a fine fighter."""
"2105","1761 - Abu Yala said: Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Miswar ibn al-Salt reported, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir reported, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Whatever a man spends upon his family, his child, and his property is recorded for him as charity. And whatever a man wards off his honor with is recorded for him as charity."" He said: ""And every spending of a believer in other than disobedience - Allah Almighty guarantees its replacement, except spending on buildings."" We said to Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): O Abu Abdullah, what did he mean by ""what a man wards off his honor with""? He said: Giving to the poet and the foul-tongued. As if he says: The one whose tongue is feared."
"2106","Chapter 42: A woman's reward when she bears a child. 1762 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak reported, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Hashim, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said - I think it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""A woman has, from her pregnancy to her delivery to her weaning, reward like one writhing in blood in the path of Allah; if she dies in between, she has the reward of a martyr."""
"2107","1763 - Abu Yala said: Wahb - he is Ibn Baqiyyah - narrated to us, Khalid reported, from Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Out of ninety-nine women, one is in Paradise and the rest in the Fire."" That weighed heavily upon those of the Emigrants present, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim woman conceives, she has the reward of one fasting, standing in prayer, in pilgrim sanctity, striving in the path of Allah Almighty. When she gives birth, she has for the first suckling the reward of giving life to a soul."""
"2108","Chapter 43: Oaths and vows. 1764 - Abu Bakr said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, Abu Farwah narrated to me, Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi narrated to me, from Abu Thalabah al-Khushani, who said - and he met him - he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed to slaughter some camels before an idol of the pre-Islamic idols? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Fulfill your vow, but do not disobey your Lord."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no fulfilling a vow involving disobedience to Allah Almighty, nor severing kinship, nor in what one does not own."""
"2109","1765 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kurayb reported, from Kurayb, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), with al-Miswar, Abdullah ibn Shaddad, and Nafi ibn Jubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both) present, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Three things have no oath in them: no oath of a child against his father, no oath of a woman against her husband, and no oath of a slave against his master."""
"2110","1766 - Al-Harith said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash reported, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Abu Atiq, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no vow involving disobedience to Allah Almighty, no oath involving severing kinship, no oath of a slave against his master, no oath of a wife with her husband, and no oath of a child with his father."""
"2111","1767 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Hushaym narrated to us, Ibn Awn reported, a Bedouin man reported, from his father, from his grandfather: That he performed Hajj with a relative tied to him (by a vow), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him and said: ""What is this?"" He said: It is a vow. ""So he commanded the tie to be cut."""
"2112","1768 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan: al-Amash narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Abu Kanaf, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever swears by the Quran owes an oath for every verse. He said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: ""Whoever swears by the Quran owes an oath for every verse, and whoever disbelieves in a letter of it has disbelieved in all of it."""
"2113","1769 - Bishr - he is Ibn al-Mufaddal - narrated to us, al-Jurayri reported, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, who said: A man said beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): By trust! He said: ""You said: By trust? You said: By trust?""... He kept repeating it until we said: Would that he fell silent!"
"2114","1770 - Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), from a woman who said: If she wears a garment from her husband it is a gift (vowed as offering). He said: ""She should offer it."" I asked al-Hasan and he said: She expiates for her oath."
"2115","1771 - Abu Yala said: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq ibn Asma narrated to us, Ubays ibn Maymun reported, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir reported, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath, it is as he says. If he says: I am a Jew - he is a Jew; if he says: I am a Christian - he is a Christian; if he says: I am a Magian - he is a Magian."""
"2116","1772 - Al-Tayalisi said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and sees another better than it - let him do what is better and expiate for his oath."""
"2117","1773 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Hushaym narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ubaydullah reported, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Whoever swears an oath and sees another better than it - let him do what is better, and there is no expiation upon him."""
"2118","1774 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Zimmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Harith reported, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani reported, from his father, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears an oath and sees another better than it - its expiation is to abandon it."""
"2119","1775 - Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Abu Mabad, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Whoever swears upon his slave to beat him, its expiation is to abandon it, and with the expiation is a good deed."""
"2120","1776/1 - Al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: ""O so-and-so, did you do such-and-such?"" He said: No, by Allah besides whom there is no god, I did not do it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew he had done it. He said to him: ""Allah has expiated your lie for you by your affirming: There is no god but Allah."""
"2121","1776/2 - Abd ibn Humayd said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Harith reported with the same."
"2122","1776/3 - Abu Yala said: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, al-Harith narrated with the same. Al-Hakim authenticated it through the way of Malik ibn Ismail, from Abu Qudamah - he is al-Harith ibn Ubayd - with it. But Hammad ibn Salamah - who is more precise than him regarding Thabit - opposed him, saying: from Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Umar. Hammad said: Thabit did not hear this from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both); between them is a man."
"2123","1777 - Abu Yala said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim or another reported, from al-Haytham ibn Humayd, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Busr ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Abid, from Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah granted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camels as booty, and he presented them. Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah, give me a mount! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No."" He asked him three times, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Allah, I will not do it,"" until four remained, lean of hump. He said: ""Take them, O Abu Musa."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, I asked you for a mount and you refused me, and swore, so I feared that some forgetfulness had entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When I swear and see that another course is better, I expiate for my oath and do what is better."""
"2124","1778 - Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Said ibn Zarbi reported, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn al-Khuzai, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group seeking mounts, and he said: ""I have nothing to mount you upon; by Allah, I will not mount you."" He said: He left us for days, then camels of charity camels were brought, so he sent to me and ordered three camels, lean of hump, for us, and we departed with them. I said to my companions: By Allah, I do not think they will be blessed for us! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore not to mount us, so perhaps he forgot; let us return to him and remind him of his oath. We returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, your oath by which you swore not to mount us? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I remembered my oath; whoever of you swears an oath and sees another better, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath."""
"2125","1779 - Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umayyah reported, from Ibn Abi al-Khuwar, freedman of Banu Amir, who said: I heard al-Harith ibn Malik ibn al-Barsa crying out among the people in the season of Hajj - Sufyan said: I know only that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is none who swears a false oath to cut off thereby the rightful property of a Muslim man but he will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him."""
"2126","1780 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shubah reported, from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Rufay Abu al-Aliyah saying: Abu Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) - said: ""We used to count among the sin for which there is no expiation the immersing oath."" He said: It was said: What is it? He said: Cutting off a man's property by his oath."
"2127","1781 - Al-Harith said: Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hisham reported, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: ""A mudd of wheat for each poor person suffices in the expiation of an oath."""
"2128","Chapter 44: Vows. 1782 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mamar, from Zayd ibn Rufay, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""A vow is an oath."""
"2129","1783 - Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yazid Abu Khalid, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) - the same."
"2130","1784 - Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, who said: A man vowed to slaughter some camels at Buwanah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Did you swear to that, and say that, while in your soul is something of the pre-Islamic affair?"" He said: No. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then slaughter them."""
"2131","1785 - Hammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Abu Said, from Abdullah ibn Malik, who said: The sister of Uqbah ibn Amir vowed to perform Hajj walking with her hair loose, so he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Command her to wear a head-cover, to ride, and to fast three days."""
"2132","1786 - Abu Bakr and Abu Yala from him said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kurayb, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from Sinan ibn Abdullah al-Juhani, who narrated to him that his aunt al-Furay'ah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died owing an unfulfilled vow; does it suffice if I fulfill it for her? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What if your mother owed a debt and you paid it - would it not be accepted from you?"" She said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then Allah Blessed and Almighty is more entitled to that!"" She said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother died owing walking to the Kabah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Can you walk for her?"" She said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then walk for your mother."""
"2133","1787 - Abu Bakr said: Shabbah narrated to us, Shubah reported, from Abu al-Juwayriyah, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Badr mentioning from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""There is no vow involving disobedience to Allah."" The hadith of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about one upon whom a sacrificial camel is due and cannot find it, that he slaughter seven sheep, has preceded in the chapter of sacrificial animals in the Book of Hajj."
"2134","1788 - Al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Fatimah bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army and said: ""If good news of them reaches me, I shall surely praise Allah Almighty with His true praise."" When good news of them reached him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""O Allah, to You is praise in gratitude, and to You is favor in bounty."" Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you said: If good news of them reaches me I shall praise Allah with His true praise? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I said: ""O Allah, to You is praise in gratitude, and to You is favor in bounty."""
"2135","Book 18: Prescribed penalties. Chapter 1: Prohibition of a Muslim's blood and honor. 1789/1 - Abu Yala said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabalah narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Numan reported, from Kathir ibn al-Fadl, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, saying: ""What day is this?"" We said: The day of sacrifice. He said: ""What month is this?"" We said: Dhu al-Hijjah, a sacred month. He said: ""Then what land is this?"" We said: A sacred land. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then your blood, your wealth, and your honor are forbidden to you as the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours! Let the witness convey to the absent."" The hadith of Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both) has preceded in the chapter on the sanctity of Makkah, and likewise the hadith of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"2136","1790 - Al-Harith said: Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Umar reported, he said: Ikrimah said: Ibn Hujayr narrated to me, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed in the Farewell Pilgrimage, saying: ""O people, what land is this?"" and he mentioned the like, adding: ""Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks."""
"2137","1791 - Abu Yala said: Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father reported, Talib ibn Salma reported, one of my family narrated to me that my grandfather narrated to him that he witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his pilgrimage, in his sermon, saying: ""Your wealth and your blood are forbidden to you as the sanctity of this land on this day. Let not... you return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks. Let the witness convey to the absent."" He said: I do not know whether I shall ever meet you here after today. O Allah, bear witness over them: Have I conveyed?"
"2138","1792 - Abu Bakr said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi reported, Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: This chapter was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the middle of the days of Tashriq at Mina during the Farewell Pilgrimage: ""When the help of Allah and the victory come..."" to its end. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew it was farewell, so he ordered his camel al-Qaswa, and it was saddled for him; he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for the people at al-Aqabah, and the people gathered to him. He praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: O people, every blood-shedding of the pre-Islamic age is void, and the first blood I void is the blood of Iyas ibn Rabiah ibn al-Harith, who was nursed among Banu Layth and Hudhayl killed him. The first usury I void is the usury of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him); yours is your principal sums - you wrong not and are not wronged... and he mentioned the hadith at length."
"2139","1793 - Abu Yala said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Hanafi reported, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab reported, he said: I heard Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Amrah, from Aishah, who said: I found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a writing: ""Among the most insolent of people is one who strikes one who did not strike him, a man who kills other than his killer, and a man who takes as master other than those who favored him; whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger, and Allah accepts from him neither devotional exchange nor ransom. And in the other: The believers' blood and wealth are equal; the lowest of them strives to grant protection. No Muslim is killed for a disbeliever, nor one under covenant while in his covenant, and people of two religions do not inherit from one another. A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt nor with her maternal aunt. There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and a woman does not travel three nights with other than a mahram."""
"2140","1794/1 - Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi al-Raqqi reported, Asbagh ibn Muhammad reported, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Shaddad, freedman of Iyad, from Wabisah - meaning Ibn Mabad, Allah willing - that he would stand among the people on the day of sacrifice or the day of breaking fast, saying: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage saying: What day is this? They said: The day of sacrifice. He said: What month is this? They said: A sacred month. He said: What land is this? They said: The town. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Then your blood, your wealth, and your honor are forbidden to you as the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet Him. O Allah, have I conveyed? Let the witness convey to the absent."" Wabisah said: So we bear witness over you as was borne witness over us."
"2141","1794/2 - Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Abu Salamah al-Khuzai reported, from Jafar ibn Burqan: He narrated to them in this hadith that Salim ibn Wabisah ibn Mabad prayed with them in al-Raqqah, mentioning this hadith of Wabisah. He said: Wabisah said: ""I bear witness over you as was borne witness over us, when you were absent and we convey to you."""
"2142","Chapter 2: The penalty for wine. 1795 - Ishaq said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fix a penalty for wine until Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) fixed forty."" Ibn Shihab said: al-Saib ibn Yazid said: ""Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) fixed eighty. Then Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) lashed eighty and forty: when a man was brought who had drunk his fill of drink he lashed him eighty, and when a man was brought who had slipped once he lashed him forty."""
"2143","1796 - Abd said: Umar ibn Said al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi reported, from Makhul, from Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: She heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advising one of his family, saying: ""And beware of wine, for it is the key to every evil..."" the hadith."
"2144","1797 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Malik: al-Zuhri narrated to me, saying: ""It reached me that Umar, Ibn Umar, and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them) used to lash forty for wine."""
"2145","1798 - Hushaym narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab reported, from al-Ala ibn Badr, who said: A man drank wine or tila - Hushaym doubted - and was brought to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: He drank only what is lawful. His saying was graver to him than what he did, so he consulted about him; they advised lashing him eighty, and it became a practice after him."
"2146","1799 - Abu Yala said: Ishaq ibn Abi Israil reported, Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sakhr al-Ifriqi informed me, from Jamil ibn Kurayb, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks wine, lash him eighty."""
"2147","1800 - Musaddad said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub reported, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: Ibn al-Nuayman was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having drunk wine, so he commanded those in the house, and they rose against him and beat him with their hands, palm stalks, and sandals. This is mursal. I said: al-Bukhari has brought it through this way, adding after Ibn Abi Mulaykah: Uqbah ibn al-Harith, and adding at its end: And I was among those who beat him."
"2148","1801 - Musaddad: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks wine, lash him; if he returns a fourth time, kill him."" Mursal."
"2149","Chapter 3: Prohibition of selling wine even if it belongs to orphans. 1802 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, who said: A man gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a waterskin of wine as a gift, and he ordered it sold. When he turned away, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded its mouth-tie, and it was opened."
"2150","1803 - Abu Yala said: Jafar ibn Humayd narrated to us, Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Isa ibn Jariyah, who said: A man used to carry wine from Khaybar and sell it to the Muslims. He carried wealth-worth of it and came with it to Madinah, where a Muslim man met him and said: O so-and-so, wine has been forbidden. So he set it down where he stopped, upon a mound, and covered it with cloths. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, it reached me that wine has been forbidden! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: Shall I return it to the one I bought it from? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Returning it is not proper. He said: Shall I gift it to one who will recompense for it? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. He said: In it is wealth of orphans under my care? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the wealth of Bahrayn comes to us, we shall compensate your orphans from their wealth. Then he called out: O people of Madinah! The man said: O Messenger of Allah, may we benefit from the skins! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Untie their mouths. So it poured until it settled in the valley's bottom."
"2151","Chapter 4: The beginning of wine's prohibition. 1804 - Al-Tayalisi said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Tawbah al-Misri, who said: I heard Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: Three verses were revealed concerning wine: the first revealed was, ""They ask you about wine and gambling..."" the verse. It was said: Has wine been forbidden? They said: O Messenger of Allah, let us benefit from it as Allah Almighty said! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent toward them. Then this verse was revealed: ""Do not approach prayer while intoxicated..."" the verse. It was said: Has wine been forbidden? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we do not drink it near prayer, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent toward them. Then was revealed: ""O you who believe, wine, gambling, idols, and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, so avoid it."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is forbidden. A waterskin from Syria was presented to a man - or two waterskins - and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)... and he mentioned the hadith."
"2152","1805 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi reported, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar reported, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Tamim al-Dari (may Allah be pleased with him): That he used to gift the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a waterskin of wine every year. When Allah Almighty revealed wine's prohibition, he came with it; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it he smiled and said: It has been forbidden after you! He said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I sell it and benefit from its price? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews; the fat of cattle and sheep was forbidden to them, so they melted it and sold it. Allah Almighty has forbidden wine and its price. This is a fair hadith."
"2153","1806 - Al-Humaydi and Ibn Abi Umar both said: Sufyan narrated to us, Salim Abu al-Nadr reported, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man used to gift the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a waterskin of wine every year. One year he gifted it after it had been forbidden, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has been forbidden! The man said: Shall I not sell it? He said: The One who forbade drinking it forbade selling it. He said: Shall I not bestow it upon the Jews? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The One who forbade it forbade bestowing it upon the Jews! He said: What shall I do with it? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour it in al-Batha."
"2154","1807 - Abu Bakr said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata, from Malik ibn al-Sabbah, from a man of Thaqif, who said: A man met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come with my merchandise. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is your merchandise? He said: Wine. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go with it to al-Batha, open its mouths, and spill it. He said: He went out with it but his soul refused, so he returned to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I and my dependents have neither fugitive nor near kin besides it! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go out with it to al-Batha, open its mouths, and spill it. He said: He did so. Then he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have done so, O Messenger of Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was seen, saying: O Allah, enrich so-and-so and the family of so-and-so from Your bounty! If a man of that household were to die, he would bequeath a thousand camels."
"2155","Chapter 5: Warning against drinking wine. 1808 - Al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Awf reported, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The drinker of wine is like a worshipper of idols; the drinker of wine is like a worshipper of al-Lat and al-Uzza."
"2156","1809/1 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Israil reported, from Thuwayr, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, little or much, Allah Almighty will give him to drink of the boiling water of Hell on the Day of Resurrection."
"2157","1809/2 - Abu Yala said: al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq reported, from Israil... the same."
"2158","1810 - Abd said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal reported, Ismail ibn Rafi narrated to me, from Sulayman, freedman of Abu Said, from Abu Said al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept prayer from a wine-drinker while any of it remains in his body."
"2159","1811 - Abu Yala said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Hiql reported, from al-Muthanna, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Iyad ibn Ghanm (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever drinks wine, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies, he goes to the Fire; if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. If he drinks a second time, his prayer is not accepted for forty days; if he dies, he goes to the Fire; if he repents, Allah Almighty accepts his repentance. If he drinks a third or fourth time, it becomes due upon Allah Almighty to give him to drink of the discharge of al-Khabal. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the discharge of al-Khabal? He said: The pus of the people of the Fire."
"2160","1812 - Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abu Mashar reported, Fudayl ibn Maysarah reported, from Abu Hariz, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), and he mentioned the like."
"2161","1813 - Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri - he is Abu Ahmad - reported, Ismail ibn Ishaq reported, from Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan: Abdullah ibn Isa, a man of Basra, reported, from Abu al-Hakam, freedman of Abu al-As, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither the child of adultery, nor one disobedient to his parents, nor a wine-addict enters Paradise. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a wine-addict? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three years, once in every year."
"2162","1814 - Musa narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus reported, Abu Hudbah reported, from al-Ashath, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves the world intoxicated enters the grave intoxicated, is raised from his grave intoxicated, is ordered to the Fire intoxicated, to a mountain called Sakran, wherein is a spring flowing with pus and blood - their food and drink as long as the heavens and earth endure."
"2163","Chapter 6: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and the explanation of tila and mixed drinks. 1815 - Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum reported, from Ibn Yasar, from Sufyan ibn Wahb al-Khawlani, who said: I was with Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) in Syria, when the protected non-Muslims said: You have charged us - or imposed upon us - to provide the Muslims honey, and we cannot find it? Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Muslims enter a land and are not settled in it, it is hard for them to drink plain water; they must have what suits them. They said: We have a drink we make from grapes, something like honey. He said: Bring it. They brought it, and he (may Allah be pleased with him) began lifting it with his finger, stretching it like honey, saying: It is as if this is camel-tar. He (may Allah be pleased with him) called for water, poured it over it, then lowered it; he drank from it and his companions drank. He said: How good this is; provide the Muslims from it. So they provided them from it. It remained as Allah willed, then a man became intoxicated from it; the Muslims rose and beat him with their sandals, saying: Intoxicated. The man said: Do not kill me; by Allah, I drank only what Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) provided us. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) stood among the people saying: O people, I am but a man; I do not permit the lawful nor forbid the unlawful, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and revelation was lifted. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) took hold of his garment, saying: I declare myself free before Allah Almighty of this - that I permit you the unlawful. Leave it, for I fear people will plunge into it; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every intoxicant is forbidden, so leave it. Then Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) would make it, then Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) would drink the sweet."
"2164","1816 - Al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I forbid you even a little of what intoxicates in large amount. I said: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar raising it, and likewise al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated it from al-Dahhak. Its chain is sound."
"2165","1817 - Al-Tayalisi said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir and Abu Ubayd both narrated to us: from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, who said: al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him) addressed us upon the pulpit of Basra, saying: The wine forbidden at Madinah is the mixture of unripe dates and ripe dates."
"2166","1818 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hujr reported, Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wail reported, from his father, from Wail ibn Hujr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jalab, no janab, no wirat, and no shighar in Islam, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"2167","1819 - Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit reported, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Usayd al-Saidi (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining fresh dates and raisins."
"2168","1820 - Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, Sufyan reported: al-Amash narrated to me, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Umm al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: I used to boil tila for Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) until two-thirds of it went and a third remained."
"2169","1821 - Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, from Imran ibn Muslim, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) used to drink tila in a pitched skin."
"2170","1822 - Yahya narrated to us: Abu Khaldah reported, from Wasil ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: Intoxication is among the major sins."
"2171","1823 - Abu Yala said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Mutamir reported, from his father, from Hanash, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks a drink until his mind departs has come to a door of the doors of major sins. I said: Al-Tirmidhi brought, with this chain, one who joins two prayers without excuse."
"2172","1824 - Abu Yala said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid reported, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad reported: Muslim ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Wahb al-Khawlani, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"2173","1825 - Ahmad ibn Mani said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban reported, from Ashath ibn Abi al-Shatha, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, who said: Abdullah used to swear that what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade when wine was forbidden - commanding its jars broken and poured out - was dates and raisins."
"2174","1826/1 - Waki narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Furat ibn Sulayman, from one who informed him, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing of Islam to be overturned is like an overturned vessel, in a drink called tila."
"2175","1826/2 - Abu Yala said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Waki reported, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Furat, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) with the same."
"2176","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hayyan, my father narrated to me, from Maryam bint Tariq, she said: I entered upon Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) in her chamber among some Ansari women, and they began asking her about vessels, so she said: O believing women, you ask about vessels, though many of them did not exist in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whatever intoxicates any of you among drinks, let her avoid it, and even if the water of her pitcher intoxicates her, let her avoid it, for every intoxicant is unlawful."
"2177","Yahya narrated to us, from Qudamah, from Jasrah, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I heard her say: I do not permit intoxication, even if it be from bread or water."
"2178","Yahya narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, that he heard al-Qasim and Salim (may Allah be pleased with them both) say, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"2179","Chapter 7: Concession regarding drinking what does not intoxicate. Abu Bakr said: Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ujaybah ibn Abd al-Hamid, from his uncle Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the delegation of Abd al-Qays came, and he said: What is wrong with you that your colors have turned yellow, your bellies have grown large, and your veins have become prominent? They said: Our chief came to you and asked you about a drink of ours that suited us, and you forbade him it, and we are in an unhealthy pestilential land. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then drink whatever is wholesome for you."
"2180","Musaddad said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Muslim al-Awar narrated, from Abu Wail, he said: I campaigned with Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) to Syria, and we stopped at a lodging, then a village chief came seeking the Commander of the Believers until he reached him. When the village chief saw Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he prostrated, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: What is this prostration? He said: This is how we treat kings! Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Prostrate to your Lord who created you! He said: O Commander of the Believers, I have prepared food for you, so come to me! Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Is there anything of the Persians pictures in your house? He said: Yes. He said: We have no need of your house, but go and send us one dish of food, and do not add to it for us. He said: So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went, and he sent him the food, and he ate from it. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to his servant: Is there any of that nabidh in your skins? He said: Yes. He said: Bring it to him; he poured it into a vessel, then smelled it and found its smell objectionable. So he poured water over it three times, then drank, then said: If anything of your drink becomes dubious to you, do with it thus."
"2181","Chapter 8: Vessels. Musaddad said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated, from Abu Hajib, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Ghifar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the naqir and the muqayyar, one of them or both, and forbade the gourd vessel and the hantamah."
"2182","Abu Yala said: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Ansari Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us with the same chain."
"2183","Musaddad said: Bishr, that is Ibn al-Mufaddal, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated, Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid the hantamah. He said: I said: What is the hantamah? He said: The green jar. And he forbade the gourd vessel, the pitched and the tar-coated vessels. He said: I said: We take jars of lead in which we make nabidh in the evening and drink it in the morning. He said: That, by Allah, is khamr! He said: I said: What then? He said: A waterskin in which we make nabidh in the morning and drink it in the evening."
"2184","Abu Yala said: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated, from al-Awzai, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I awaited the breaking of the fast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and brought him nabidh of a jar. When he brought it near his mouth, it was fizzing, so he said: Strike it against the wall, for this is the drink of one who does not believe in Allah and the Last Day."
"2185","And with the same chain to al-Walid, from Sadaqah, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah, that he heard Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) report that he brought the Prophet (peace be upon him) nabidh of a jar, and he said to him the like of that."
"2186","Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Ashath ibn Umayr al-Abdi, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when they intended to leave they said: You have memorized from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) everything you heard from him, so ask him about nabidh. They came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in an unhealthy land, nothing suits us therein except drink! He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is your drink? They said: Nabidh. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In what do you drink it? They said: In the naqir. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do not drink in the naqir. They went out from him and said: By Allah, our people will not agree with us upon this, so they returned and asked him, and he said to them the like of that. Then they returned again, and he said to them: Do not drink in the naqir, lest a man among you strike his cousin a blow from which he will remain lame until the Day of Resurrection. He said: So they laughed. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you laugh at? They said: O Messenger of Allah, by Him who sent you with the truth, we drank in a naqir of ours, then some of us rose against others and this one was struck a blow from which he remained lame until the Day of Resurrection."
"2187","Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with the same."
"2188","Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated, al-Hajjaj ibn Hassan narrated, al-Muthanna al-Abdi Abu Munazil, one of Banu Ghanm, narrated, from al-Ashajj al-Asari, he said: He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a company of Abd al-Qays to visit him, and they advanced. When they arrived, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised himself for them, and they made their mounts kneel, and the people hastened. They wore only their travel clothes, while al-Asari stood and tied the mounts of his companions and his own camel. Then he took out his clothes from his bag, and that was before the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he came forward greeting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Abd al-Qays, why do I see your faces changed? They said: O Prophet of Allah, we are in an unhealthy land, and we used to take from these nabidhs what cuts the pieces of meat in our bellies, and when you forbade us vessels we stopped; that is what you see in our faces. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Vessels neither permit nor forbid, but every intoxicant is unlawful, and it is not that you sit and drink until, when the veins are filled, you boast, then a man leaps upon his cousin and strikes him with the sword, leaving him lame. He said: And he was that day among the people the lame one who was afflicted by that. Ibn Hibban declared it authentic."
"2189","Al-Tayalisi said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I asked Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) about nabidh of the jar? He said: I did not hear anything about it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to dislike it."
"2190","Abu Yala said: Ahmad, that is al-Dawraqi, narrated to us, al-Tayalisi narrated with the same."
"2191","He said: And Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Harami narrated, Shubah narrated with the same in abridged form."
"2192","Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated, Asim ibn Umar narrated, he said: I asked Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and others besides me asked him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid nabidh of the jar? He said: How could he have forbidden it? By Allah, he never saw it at all!"
"2193","Abu Bakr said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Yasar, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Suhar al-Abdi, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a sickly man, so permit me a jar in which to make nabidh, and he permitted me therein."
"2194","Al-Harith said: al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: And I heard him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), forbidding nabidh of the jar, and I heard him when he commanded drinking nabidh of the jar."
"2195","Book of Hudud, continuation. Chapter 9: Making nabidh in waterskins, and the basis of that. Al-Tayalisi said: Uyaynah narrated to us, my father, that is Abd al-Rahman ibn Jawshan, informed me, he said: Nabidh used to be made for Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) in a jar, then Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) came from an absence he had been absent, and stopped at the house of Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) before coming to his own house, and stood over a woman called Mayyah, and asked her about Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) and his condition, and looked and saw the jar in which was the nabidh, and said: What is this jar? She said: We make nabidh for Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: I wish you had put it in a waterskin. Then he went out, and the woman ordered the nabidh to be transferred into a waterskin, then she hung it. Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) came, and she informed him about Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) and his arrival, then he saw the waterskin and said: I will not drink from it; if you put honey in a jar it would become unlawful for me, and if you put khamr in a waterskin it would become lawful for me? We have known what we were forbidden: we were forbidden the gourd vessel, the naqir, the hantam and the tar-coated vessel. As for the gourd, we were a people of Thaqif at Taif, we used to take the gourd and hollow out in it clusters of grapes, then bury it, then leave it until it ferments, then it dies. As for the naqir, the people of Yamamah used to hollow the base of the palm tree, and split therein fresh and unripe dates, then leave it until it ferments, then it dies. As for the hantam, they are jars that used to be carried to us in which was khamr. As for the muzaffat, they are these vessels in which is pitch."
"2196","Musaddad said: Ismail narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yazid narrated, both said: Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us with the same."
"2197","Al-Bazzar said: Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated, from Uyaynah, with the same."
"2198","Chapter 10: The ruling on the apostate. Musaddad said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asking him about a man who became Muslim then disbelieved, then became Muslim then disbelieved, thereafter several times: is Islam accepted from him? Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to him: Accept from them what Allah has accepted from them; present Islam to him, and if he accepts, otherwise strike his neck."
"2199","Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan narrated, Imran ibn Zibyan narrated, from a man of Banu Hanifah, he said: Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: Do you know al-Rajjal? I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: His molar tooth in the Fire will be greater than Uhud. He had become Muslim, then apostatized and joined Musaylimah, and said: Two rams butted, and the dearest to me is that my ram wins."
"2200","Abu Yala said: al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated, Mujalid narrated, from Amir, that is al-Shabi, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and those who apostatized apostatized, Adi ibn Hatim stood with a thousand men of Tayy, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent Khalid ibn al-Walid (may Allah be pleased with him) to al-Yamamah. He said: And Banu Amir had killed the officials of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and burned them with fire, so Abu Bakr wrote to Khalid (may Allah be pleased with them both): Kill Banu Amir and burn them with fire, and he did until the women screamed. Then he proceeded until he reached the water, and they came out to him, and he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, and they said: We bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and we bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and when he heard that he refrained from them."
"2201","Chapter 11: Prohibition of the blood of the Muslim, especially when he has prayed. Muadh ibn al-Muthanna said in the additions to the Musnad: Makin al-Hazim narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, he said: When al-Hajjaj besieged Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him), he seized a man and handed him to Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) to kill him, so Salim said to him: Are you a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: And did you pray the morning prayer? He said: Yes. He said: Go, I have no way against you. What he did reached al-Hajjaj, so he said to him: What did you do with the man? He said: I asked him: Are you a Muslim? He said: Yes, and I asked him: Did you pray the morning prayer? He said: Yes, and my father informed me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that: Whoever prays the morning prayer is in the protection of Allah Almighty until morning or evening. He said: He is among the killers of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: I am not the guardian of Uthman to kill his killers. It reached his father Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he went out hurrying, dragging his waist-wrapper, and met him for what he had done, and said: I named you Salim that you be safe; I named you Salim that you be safe."
"2202","Chapter 12: Expelling the apostates after seeking their repentance. Ishaq said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: A man passed by a mosque of the mosques of Banu Hanifah, and their imam was reciting with the recitation of Musaylimah: By the grinders grinding, and the kneaders kneading, and the tharid-makers making tharid, and the morsel-swallowers swallowing, so Abd Allah sent and they were brought, and they were seventy reciting upon the recitation of Musaylimah, so Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We are not those who secure Satan, these; move them to Syria, that Allah Almighty may annihilate them by stabbing and plague. I say: The story of these was narrated by Abu Dawud and others from the narration of Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him), and there is nothing in it of what is here."
"2203","Chapter 13: Until when is the repentance of the apostate accepted. Abu Yala said: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariya narrated, from al-Mualla, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought the repentance of a man who apostatized from Islam four times."
"2204","Chapter 14: Sodomy. Al-Harith said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariya narrated to us, Mujalid narrated, from al-Shabi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, what a good people your nation is, were it not that among them are remnants of the deed of the people of Lut."
"2205","Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abbad narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the pulpit: Whoever does the deed of the people of Lut, kill him."
"2206","Chapter 15: How confession of adultery is made and the rulers questioning of the confessor, leaving the confessor if he retracts, warning against adultery, and therein: mention of the child of adultery. Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Muslim al-Awar, from Habbah ibn Juwayn, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A woman came to him and said: I committed adultery. He said: Perhaps you were approached while you were sleeping in your bed, or were you coerced? She said: I was approached willingly, not coerced. He said: Perhaps you were overpowered against yourself? She said: I was not angered. So he detained her, and when she gave birth and her son grew up, he flogged her."
"2207","Abu Bakr said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ibn Iyad, from Isa ibn Hittan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The children of adultery will be gathered in the form of monkeys and pigs."
"2208","Al-Tayalisi said: Talhah al-Ama narrated to us, from a man he named, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the youths of Quraysh: Do not commit adultery, for whoever Allah Almighty preserves his youth for him will enter Paradise. Al-Bazzar brought it out through the path of al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), and said: We do not know it with this wording except with this chain."
"2209","Musaddad said: Hafs narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, he said: A woman confessed before Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) to adultery, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent Abu Waqid and said: If you retract we will leave you, but she refused, so he stoned her."
"2210","Chapter 16: Warning against adultery, sodomy, procuring, slander and drinking khamr. Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated, from Abu Aishah al-Sadi, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Huraira and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), they both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, and they mentioned the hadith, and therein: And whoever marries a woman in her anus, or a man or a boy, will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection stinking more than carrion, people will be harmed by him until he enters Hell, and Allah will nullify his reward, and Allah will not accept from him obligatory nor voluntary worship, and he will be entered into a coffin of fire, and iron nails will be unleashed upon him until those nails interlock in his belly; if a vein of his veins were placed upon four hundred nations they would all die, and he is among the people of the Fire most severe in punishment on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever commits adultery with a Muslim or non-Muslim woman, free or slave, three hundred thousand gates of the Fire will be opened upon him in his grave, from which will come out upon him snakes, scorpions and blazes of fire, and he will be punished until the Day of Resurrection with that fire, along with what he meets of those snakes and scorpions, and he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection with people harmed by his private part, and he will be known by that until he enters the Fire, and the people of the Fire will be harmed by him, along with what they are in of punishment. Indeed Allah Almighty forbade sacred things, and none is more jealous than Allah Almighty, and of His jealousy He forbade indecencies and set the hudud. Whoever shakes hands with an unlawful woman will come on the Day of Resurrection with his hands chained to his neck, then he will be commanded to the Fire. If he jests with her, he will be detained for every word he spoke to her in the world a thousand years. And the woman, if she obeys the man and he embraces her or kisses her or touches her or jests with her or has intercourse with her, upon her is of sin like what is upon the man; if the man overpowers her against herself, upon him is his sin and her sin. Whoever casts at chaste women or a chaste woman, his deed is nullified and he will be flogged on the Day of Resurrection seventy thousand from before him and from behind him, then he will be commanded to the Fire. Whoever drinks khamr in the world, Allah Almighty will give him to drink of the venom of black snakes and the venom of scorpions a drink by which the flesh of his face falls into the vessel before he drinks it; when he drinks it, his flesh and skin rot like carrion, the people of the gathering are harmed by him, then he will be commanded to the Fire. Lo, its drinker, presser, one for whom it is pressed, seller, buyer, carrier, one to whom it is carried, and eater of its price are equal in its sin and disgrace, and neither fasting nor hajj nor umrah will be accepted from him until he repents; if he dies before repenting from it, it is right upon Allah Almighty to give him for every sip he drank in the world a drink of the pus of Hell. Lo, every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful. Whoever procures between two men and an unlawful woman, Allah forbids him Paradise, and his abode is the Fire, an evil destination. Whoever describes a woman to a man and mentions to him her beauty and loveliness until he is fascinated by her and attains from her a need, he leaves the world wrathfully dealt with; whoever Allah is wrathful with, the seven heavens and seven earths are wrathful with him, and upon him is of sin like that which befell her. We said: If they both repent and amend? He said: It will be accepted from them both, but it will not be accepted from the one who described her. Whoever commits immorality with a married woman, a valley of pus a five-hundred-year journey bursts from her private part, the people of the Fire are harmed by its stinking wind, and he will be among the people most severe in punishment on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever gains power over an unlawful woman or slave girl and leaves her for Allah Almighty fearing Him, Allah Blessed and Almighty secures him from the greatest terror, forbids him to the Fire, and enters him into Paradise; if he has intercourse with her unlawfully, Allah forbids him Paradise and enters him into the Fire. This is a fabricated hadith, and the accused of it is Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi."
"2211","Al-Tayalisi said: Shubah narrated to us, a man of the family of Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ammar, from Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pimp will not enter Paradise."
"2212","Chapter 18: Averting the hadd by doubt. Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, Shubah narrated, from Asim, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Avert the hudud from the servants of Allah Almighty. (79) And the hadith of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) will come, Allah willing, in theft."
"2213","Chapter 20: The hadd is obligatory upon the sick. Abu Bakr said: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Umar ibn Ata, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A servant girl of the family of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed immorality, so he said: O Ali, apply the hadd to her. He said: So he left her until she delivered what was in her belly, then lashed her fifty, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: You did right."
"2214","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, that is Ibn Amr ibn Hazm, narrated to me, from his father, he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) applied the hadd upon a man while he was sick, and said: I fear he may die before the hadd is applied upon him."
"2215","Chapter 21: Lesbianism. Abu Yala said: Abu Hammam narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Anbasah ibn Said, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intimacy of women with women is adultery among them."
"2216","Chapter 22: The ruling on one who confesses to an unspecified hadd. Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Nusayr ibn Dhuluq narrated to me, from Khulayd, he said: A man came to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: I have incurred a hadd, so Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Ask him, what is it? But they did not inform them, so Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Beat him until he forbids you."
"2217","Chapter 23: One who does less than the hadd. Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Amya narrated to me, he said: Sahl ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl narrated to him: That he and his father entered upon Anas (may Allah be pleased with him). He mentioned the hadith, he said: Then they went early the next morning and said: We ride to look and reflect. He said: Yes. So they all rode, and there they were by ruined dwellings whose people had perished and vanished, and they remained empty upon their roofs. They said: Do you know these dwellings? He said: How well I know them and their people; these are the people of dwellings whom transgression and envy destroyed; envy extinguishes the light of good deeds, and transgression confirms that or belies it, and the eye commits adultery, and likewise the palm, the foot, the hand and the tongue, and the private part confirms that or belies it."
"2218","Chapter 24: Stoning. (81) The hadith of Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) on stoning will come, Allah willing, in the exegesis of al-Maidah. Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sulaym, from Najih Abu Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) stoned, and the command of the two of them is sunnah."
"2219","Chapter 25: Mutah. Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, I heard Nafi narrate, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Had I preceded in the matter of mutah of women, I would have stoned."
"2220","Chapter 26: The hadd of theft. Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Abd Rabbihi ibn Abi Umayyah informed me, that al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabiah and Ibn Sabit al-Ahwal both narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a slave and it was said: This one stole, and proof was established against him, and his stolen goods were found with him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a slave of orphans who have none besides him, so he left him. Then he was brought a second time, and a third, then a fourth, and he left him four times. Then he was brought a fifth time and he cut his hand, then he was brought a sixth time and he cut his foot, then a seventh and he cut his hand, then an eighth and he cut his foot. Then al-Harith said: Four for four; he pardoned him four times and punished him four times. This is mursal; al-Harith and Ibn Sabit have no companionship."
"2221","Al-Harith said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me with the same."
"2222","And he said: And Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Umayyah, from al-Harith ibn Abd Allah with the same. And likewise Abu Dawud brought it out in al-Marasil from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari, from Hammad ibn Masadah. And al-Baghawi said in his Mujam: Harun ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Masadah narrated with the same."
"2223","Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn al-Hadrami: That he brought to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) a slave boy of his who had stolen. He said: He stole a mirror of my family, and it is better than sixty dirhams. He said: Your servant took your goods."
"2224","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, that is al-Thawri, Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had stolen a shawl, and he said: Did you steal? I do not think you steal. He said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take him and cut his hand, then cauterize it, then bring him to me. So they cut it, then cauterized it, then brought him, and he said: Repent to Allah. He said: I repent to Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, turn to him. Abu Dawud narrated it in al-Marasil from Ahmad ibn Abdah, from Sufyan, that is Ibn Uyaynah, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, thus. And al-Bazzar narrated it from Ahmad ibn Aban, from Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, and said therein: I see it only from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him). And al-Daraqutni narrated it through the path of Yaqub al-Dawraqi from al-Darawardi with mention of Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) without doubt. Al-Daraqutni said: And it has reached me that Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated it from Yazid ibn Khusayfah connected."
"2225","Al-Harith said: Ashhal, that is Ibn Hatim, narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated, from al-Hasan, he said: A man brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a man leading him who had stolen a cloak, and he commanded his hand to be cut, so the man said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not know that my cloak would reach what a Muslim mans hand is cut for. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then would that this had been before. This is mursal; its men are trustworthy."
"2226","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both) was brought a young servant of Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabiah who had stolen, so he commanded him and he was measured by spans, and found six spans, so he cut him. And he narrated to us that to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was written about a boy of the people of Iraq who had stolen, so he wrote: If you find him six spans, cut him; they found him six spans lacking a fingertip, so he was left and named Numaylah."
"2227","Abu Bakr said: Abdah narrated to us, Yahya narrated, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought a boy who had stolen, so he commanded him and he was measured by spans, and found six spans except a fingertip, so he left him and he was named Numaylah."
"2228","Musaddad said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I do not cut more than a hand and a foot."
"2229","Ahmad ibn Mani said: al-Haytham, that is Ibn Kharijah, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated, from Haram ibn Uthman, from Muadh ibn Abd Allah ibn Khubayb, he said: Abd Allah al-Juhani, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever steals, cut his hand, then if he steals, cut his foot, then if he steals, cut his hand, then if he steals, cut his foot."
"2230","Abu Yala said: Ubayd Allah, that is al-Qawariri, narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated, Abu al-Muhayyah narrated, he said: Abu Matar said: I saw Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) brought a man, and they said: He stole a camel. He said: I do not see you stole. He said: Yes indeed. He said: Perhaps it was made dubious to you? He said: Yes indeed, I stole. He said: Take him, O Qanbar, tie his finger and kindle the fire, and call the butcher to cut, then wait until I come. When he came he said to him: Did you steal? He said: No, so he left him. They said: O Commander of the Believers, why did you leave him when he had confessed to you? He said: I take him by his word and leave him by his word. Then Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had stolen, and he commanded his hand to be cut, then he wept. We said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you weep? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And how should I not weep while my nation is cut among you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, would you not have pardoned him? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is an evil ruler who pardons hudud, but overlook the hudud among yourselves."
"2231","Chapter 27: Rebuke against sitting on the bed of a woman whose husband is absent. Abu Yala said: Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated, Sharik narrated, from al-Amash, from Khaythamah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), raised: The likeness of one who sits on the bed of a woman whose husband is absent is like one whom lions bite on the Day of Resurrection."
"2232","Al-Harith said: Ashhal ibn Hatim narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, he said: A man came from those branches to Umar, and spread his quiver, and a sheet fell, and in it was: My waist-wrapper... captive she-camels... Jadah... hobbled... behind. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Call Jadah ibn Sulaym. They called him and he spoke to him, and he commanded him, and he struck him a hundred while bound, and forbade him to enter upon a woman whose husband is absent."
"2233","Chapter 28: Disciplining one who slanders the imam. Ishaq said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: I heard my father say: Abu Nadrah narrated, from Abu Said, freedman of Abu Usayd, he said: Some people were at the tent of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), I think that at Makkah, and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by them. Abu Said (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No one of the people remained except he cursed him or reviled him besides me, and among those who cursed him or reviled him was a man of the people of Kufa. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) was severest against the Kufan besides others, and said: O Kufan, do you revile me? As if threatening him. He said: Then he came to Madinah, and it was said to him, meaning to the Kufan: Upon you is Talhah. Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) went with him until he came to Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah, I shall flog you a hundred. He said: Talhah said: By Allah, you shall not flog him unless he be an adulterer. He said: I shall deprive you of your stipend. Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Kufan, Allah will provide for you."
"2234","Chapter 29: Silencing one who oversteps against the imam. And with this chain he said: There was some matter between Uthman and Aisha (may Allah be pleased with them both), and each of them addressed his companion, and Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) went to speak, so Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said takbir and the people said takbir with him, and he did that with her twice so that her speech would not be heard. When she saw that, she fell silent."
"2235","Chapter 30: The measure of discretionary punishment. Al-Harith said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Hisham narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Muhajir ibn Ikrimah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for one who believes in Allah and the Last Day to flog more than ten lashes except in a hadd."
"2236","And Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated, Yahya narrated, from al-Muhajir ibn Ikrimah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham: That he narrated to him, and he had servants in a village of the villages of Rome, and they fought, so he struck each of them three lashes. Then he mentioned the hadith similarly. This is mursal; its men are trustworthy."
"2237","Chapter 31: Expelling suspicious and sinful people from houses. Abu Bakr said: Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father Sad ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: He proposed to a woman at Makkah while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Would that I had one who saw her and who informs about her. A man called Hit said: I shall describe her to you; when she approaches, you say: she walks upon six, and when she turns away, you say: she walks upon four. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I see this as evil; I see he knows the affair of women. He used to enter upon her, meaning upon Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her), and when he came to Madinah he exiled him, and he was thus until the rule of Umar, who used to permit him to enter Madinah on Friday to give charity."
"2238","Abu Yala said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with the same. And al-Bazzar brought it out from Mahmud ibn Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, and added after his saying: And this one knows women, and he used to enter upon Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her): so he forbade her that he enter upon her, and said at its end: So he gives charity every Friday. Al-Bazzar said: We know no one who narrated it from Sad except his son, nor from him except Mujahid, nor from him except Abd al-Karim, nor from him except Ibn Abi Layla, nor from him except Isa, nor from him except Bakr, and Mujahid narrated in musnad form from Amir ibn Sad only this hadith."
"2239","Chapter 32: Imprisonment. Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil narrated to us, Ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak narrated, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imprisoned on suspicion as precaution and corroboration for a day and a night."
"2240","Chapter 33: Slander. Musaddad said: Hafs narrated to us, from Ashath, from al-Hasan, he said: A man said to a man: You do not approach your wife except by adultery or unlawfully, so he raised him to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He has slandered you with a matter lawful to you."
"2241","Book 19: Retaliation. Chapter 1: Retaliation for one killed with a stone. Musaddad said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Mirdas, he said: A man threw a stone at a man and killed him, so he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he retaliated from him. Muhammad ibn Jabir is weak. And Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated it from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah: Our shaykhs who reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us. He mentioned it. And there is criticism of Hajjaj. And al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr followed him, from Ziyad, from Mirdas ibn Urwah, he said: A man of the tribe threw at a brother of his and killed him, and fled, and we found him with Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him), and we went with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he retaliated from him. Ibn al-Sakan brought it out in al-Sahabah, and al-Bukhari mentioned it in al-Tarikh. He said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah said: al-Walid narrated with it. And its chain is good."
"2242","Chapter 2: One from whom retaliation is not taken in this world will have it taken from him in the Hereafter. Abu Bakr said: Waki narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Ibn Judan, from his grandmother, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a servant girl of his and she was late, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for fear of retaliation on the Day of Resurrection, I would have hurt you with this siwak."
"2243","Abu Yala said: al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Waki narrated with the same."
"2244","And Abu Yala also said: Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father narrated, from Dawud, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Judan, from his grandmother, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in my house, and in his hand was a siwak, and he called a servant girl of his or hers until anger became evident in his face. Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) went out to the open ground and found the servant girl playing with a young sheep, and said: Do I not see you playing with this young sheep while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you? She said: No, by Him who sent you with the truth, I did not hear you. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for fear of retaliation, I would have hurt you with this siwak."
"2245","Chapter 3: Retaliation in other than life. Musaddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both) retaliated for a slap."
"2246","Abu Bakr said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man stabbed a man with a horn in his knee, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking retaliation, and it was said to him: Until you heal. He refused and hastened and took retaliation. He said: So his leg became defective, while the leg of the one retaliated against healed. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said to him: You have nothing; you refused. Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah followed him from Ismail. And al-Daraqutni said: The two sons of Abi Shaybah erred therein. Ahmad narrated it from Ibn Ulayyah, from the mursal of Amr ibn Dinar, and it is the preserved from Amr."
"2247","Musaddad said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Said narrated, Qatadah narrated, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated to them that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say regarding one from whom retaliation is taken then he dies: His killing is right; no blood-money."
"2248","And from Qatadah, from Khilas, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Book of Allah Almighty: That he has no blood-money."
"2249","And from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say therein: There is deducted from him the measure of his wound, then he is liable for what remains."
"2250","Chapter 4: Prohibition of mutilation. Ishaq said: Jarir informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Qays ibn al-Ahnaf, from Asma bint Abi Bakr: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mutilation. I say: I did not know Qays ibn al-Ahnaf who he is; the known is al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, but Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad did not reach him."
"2251","Chapter 5: Blood-money. Ishaq said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Aslam, freedman of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), standing upon this pulpit teaching people the sunnahs, and among what he taught them he said: For the collarbone a camel, for the molar tooth a camel, and for the rib a camel."
"2252","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Muslim ibn Jundub, that he heard his father Aslam say: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) say: For the molar tooth a camel, and for the collarbone a camel."
"2253","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Jazari informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed me, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) used to assign for the thumb and the one next to it half the blood-money of the hand, and assign for the thumb fifteen, for the one next to it ten, for the middle ten, for the one next to it nine, and for the other six, until Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) came, and found a letter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had written to Amr ibn Hazm, therein: And for the fingers ten ten, so Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) made them ten ten."
"2254","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi informed us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib say: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) decreed for the thumb and the one next to it half the blood-money of the hand, for the middle ten, for the one next to it nine, and for the little finger six. Said said: Until he found a letter with the family of Amr ibn Hazm, they claim it is from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), therein: And for every finger ten. Said said: So it became ten ten. This is a sound connected chain to Ibn al-Musayyib; if he heard it from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), then that is it."
"2255","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) about a one-eyed man whose sound eye was put out? Abd Allah ibn Safwan said: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) decreed therein the blood-money. He said: You I ask. He said: You ask me, while this one informs you that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) decreed that?"
"2256","Abu Bakr said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, he said: I met Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was at the season, and I called from behind the tent: Lo, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so al-Jarmi, and a nephew of ours has a brother captive among so-and-so, and we presented to him the ordinance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he refused. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) raised the side of the tent and said: Do you know your companion? I said: Yes. He said: There he is; go with him until we execute for you two the decree of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And we used to relate that it was four camels."
"2257","Musaddad said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used not to let maternal brothers inherit from the blood-money."
"2258","Abu Yala said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Muadh narrated, my father narrated, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali, he said: Maternal brothers do not inherit the blood-money of their maternal brother when he is killed."
"2259","Ishaq said: Yahya informed us, Ibn Lahiah informed me, from Muadh ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, from Uqbah ibn Suhban, he said: Amr ibn Madi Karib struck a man of Banu Kinanah with a head wound reaching the brain, and Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wanted to retaliate from him, so al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no retaliation in a mamumah. This is a weak chain and in it is a break. And Ibn Majah brought out from it the raised portion."
"2260","Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated, Ibn Lahiah narrated with the same."
"2261","Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from a man he named, from another man of Thaqif he named, he said: While I was with Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), a bedouin came seeking a head wound, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We, the people of villages, do not mutually bear the mudghah among us."
"2262","Al-Harith said: al-Waqidi narrated to us, Musa ibn Shaybah narrated, from Kharijah ibn Abd Allah ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: We were in our ignorance, and we used to bear of the blood-money only what reached a third of the blood-money, and it was taken immediately; if it was not found with us it was like a debt continuing. When Islam came, among what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laid down from the aqilah of Quraysh and the Ansar was a third of the blood-money."
"2263","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said regarding quasi-intentional: Striking with a stick, and a heavy stone, in thirds: a third jidha, a third hiqqah, and a third thaniyyah to bazil of its year. Yazid said: I know it only said: pregnant."
"2264","Abu Bakr said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated, Mujalid narrated, al-Shabi narrated, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Two women of Hudhayl, one of them killed the other. He mentioned the hadith, he said: And she was pregnant, so the aqilah of the killed said: She was pregnant and cast a fetus, and the aqilah of the killer feared they would be charged, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, he neither drank nor ate, nor cried out and uttered a cry. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the rhymed speech of ignorance. So he decreed for the fetus a ghurrah, a slave or slave girl. I say: Its basis is with Abu Dawud. And Salamah ibn Tammam narrated it from Abu al-Malih, from his father, connected."
"2265","Al-Tabarani said in al-Kabir: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said al-Murri narrated, al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated, from Salamah ibn Tammam, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah, from his father, he said: There was among us a man called Hamal ibn Malik who had two wives: one Hudhali, the other Amiri, and the Hudhali struck the Amiri with a tent pole or tent peg, and she cast a dead fetus. The striker was taken to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a brother of hers called Imran ibn Uwaymir. He mentioned it and added therein: Or five hundred, or a horse. Imran said: O Prophet of Allah, she has two sons who are chiefs of the tribe, and they are more entitled to bear for their mother. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are more entitled to bear for your sister than her children. He said: I have nothing with which to bear. He said: O Hamal ibn Malik, and he was that day over the charities of Hudhayl, and he was the husband of the two women and the father of the killed fetus: Take from under your hand of the charities of Hudhayl a hundred and twenty sheep. So he did."
"2266","And Abu Nuaym said: al-Tabarani narrated to us with it. And Ibn Mandah narrated it through the path of Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from al-Minhal with it, similarly but abridged, and therein: So he said: Give it to her brother Imran ibn Uwaymir. He said: Give one who neither ate... the hadith."
"2267","And al-Tabarani said: Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated, Abbad ibn Mansur narrated, Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali narrated, from Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabighah, that he had two wives: Lihyani and Muawiyah of Banu Muawiyah ibn Zayd, and they met and became jealous, so the Muawiyah raised a stone and threw the Lihyani while she was pregnant, and she perished and killed her and cast a boy. Hamal ibn Malik said to Imran ibn Uwaymir: Give me the blood-money of my wife. They rose to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The blood-money is upon the asabah."
"2268","Al-Harith said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Said narrated, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, he said: Hamal ibn al-Nabighah had two wives: Mulaykah and Umm Afif, and one of them threw the other with a stone and it struck her heart, and she cast a dead fetus. That was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he decreed that the blood-money is upon the people of the aqilah of the killer, and for the fetus a ghurrah: a slave or slave girl, or ten camels, or a hundred sheep. Her guardian or her father said: O Messenger of Allah, he neither ate nor drank, nor cried out and uttered a cry, so the like of that is void. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not of the rhymes of ignorance in anything."
"2269","Abu Yala said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated, I heard Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, I heard Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman narrate from Aisha, she said: I found in the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a writing: That among the most insolent of people is one who strikes other than his striker, and a man who kills other than his killer, and a man who takes as master other than his benefactor; whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger, nothing obligatory nor voluntary will be accepted from him. And in requital: The believers, their blood and property are equal, and the lowest of them strives for their protection; no Muslim is killed for a disbeliever, nor one of covenant in his covenant, nor do people of two religions inherit from one another, nor is a woman married upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt, nor prayer after Asr until the sun sets, nor does a woman travel three nights with other than a mahram."
"2270","Chapter 6: Blood-money in accidental killing and pardon therein. Musaddad said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, Mujalid narrated, an arif of Juhaynah narrated to me: That some people of Juhaynah brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a captive among the captives, and he said: Go with him and warm him. He said: Warming in their tongue was killing. So they went with him and killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked them, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, you commanded us to kill him and we killed him. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did I say to you? They said: You said to us: Go with him and warm him. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have shared with you; then pay his blood-money, and I am your partner. Mujalid said: So I narrated this hadith to Amir, meaning al-Shabi, and he said: He spoke truth, and knew the hadith."
"2271","Al-Harith said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, he said: The Muslims mistakenly killed Abu Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) on the day of Uhud, and he kept saying: My father, my father, until they killed him. He said: May Allah forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of the merciful. It reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it increased him in good with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood-money from himself."
"2272","And with the same to Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, similarly, except he said: So he commanded him and he was paid for. I say: This story is in al-Bukhari from Urwah, and I did not see therein his saying: So he was paid for."
"2273","Musaddad said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Uqbah, from Yazid ibn Madhkur, he said: A man was crushed on Friday and died, so Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) paid his blood-money from the public treasury."
"2274","Abu Bakr said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Imran ibn Zibyan, from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: A man smashed the mouth of a man in the time of Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), and the blood-money was offered to him but he refused it, and they increased him until they gave him three blood-moneys. He said: Then a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives charity of blood or less than it, it will be expiation for what preceded of his sins from the day his mother bore him until the day he gives it in charity. He said: So the man pardoned."
"2275","Abu Yala said: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated with the same."
"2276","Chapter 7: The measure of blood-money and its valuation. Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, he said: The blood-money in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was four ages: twenty-five hiqqah, twenty-five jadhah, twenty-five daughters of labun, and twenty-five daughters of makhad, until Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came and founded the garrison cities. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Not all people find camels, so value the camels an ounce an ounce; so it was four thousand. Then camels became dear, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Value the camels; they were valued an ounce and a half. He said: So it was six thousand. Then camels became dear, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Value the camels; they were valued two ounces, so it was eight thousand. Then camels became dear, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Value the camels; they were valued two ounces and a half, so it was ten thousand. Then camels became dear, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Value the camels; the camels were valued three ounces, so it was twelve thousand. So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) assigned upon the people of silver twelve thousand, upon the people of gold a thousand dinars, upon the people of camels a hundred camels, upon the people of garments two hundred hullah, the value of every hullah five dinars, upon the people of sheep a thousand sheep, upon the people of goats two thousand goats, and upon the people of cattle two hundred cows. Abu Mashar and his shaykh are weak."
"2277","Chapter 8: The highway robber. Abd ibn Humayd said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated, Kathir ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghatafani narrated, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Said al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what of one who meets me wanting to take my property? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adjure him by Allah Almighty three times; if he refuses, fight him. If he kills you, you enter Paradise, and if you kill him, he enters the Fire."
"2278","Book 20: Jihad. (82) The hadith of Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) on the virtue of jihad and martyrdom is at the beginning of the hadiths of the prophets. Chapter 1: Martyrs. Ishaq said: Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us, Badr ibn Uthman narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to me, from Sad (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We were with one of the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day in an illness he was ill, while he was unconscious, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and said: What were you in just now? He said: We mentioned the martyrs of this nation; we see them only as one who goes out with his property until he is killed. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my nation are few; they are martyred by killing, plague, drowning, belly disease, a womans death in childbed together, and her death in her postpartum."
"2279","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us, Aban ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali narrated, Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad narrated to me, he said: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas disputed with Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) over property of his, and Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to him one day while Sad (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting with his sword unsheathed, placing it upon his thighs. Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: For whom have you prepared this, O Sad? He said: For you. He said: Would you do it? He said: By Him who sent Muhammad with the truth, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fights for his property or property of his and is killed is a martyr."
"2280","And Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Aban ibn Abd Allah narrated with the same."
"2281","Ishaq said: Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, Amr ibn Marzuq, meaning al-Washihi, narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Rafi ibn Khadij narrated to me, from his grandmother (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Rafi ibn Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) was struck on the day of Uhud in his breast by an arrow, and he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Remove the arrow. He said: If you wish, I remove the arrow and the cotton, and if you wish, I remove the arrow and leave the cotton, and I bear witness for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr? He said: I said: Remove the arrow and leave the cotton, and bear witness for me on the Day of Resurrection that I am a martyr. He said: Yes. So he removed the arrow and left the cotton. He lived the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them), and when the time of Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) or after it came, he died after Asr. They wanted to take him out. Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: One like Rafi ibn Khadij is not taken out until those around us of the villages are informed. He sat from the morrow, and when the morrow came he was taken out. A freedwoman of his wept at the edge of the grave, and Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The shaykh has no strength for the punishment of Allah Almighty from this foolish woman, or a word like it."
"2282","Al-Tayalisi said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, and mentioned part of it."
"2283","Ahmad ibn Mani said: Yazid narrated to us, Juwaybir narrated, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one killed defending his family is a martyr, and the one killed defending his neighbor is a martyr, and every one killed in the cause of Allah Almighty is a martyr."
"2284","Al-Harith said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Juwaybir narrated, and mentioned it with the wording: Whoever is killed defending his property wrongfully is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending himself is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his family is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his neighbor is a martyr, and whoever is killed in the cause of Allah Almighty is a martyr. In it is a break."
"2285","Abu Yala said: Amr narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated, Harun ibn Hayyan narrated, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr."
"2286","Abu Yala said: Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated, from Umar ibn Malik, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar, from Jafar ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is thrown from his mount in the cause of Allah Almighty and dies is a martyr."
"2287","Abu Bakr said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from a man, from Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The passing of my nation is by stabbing and plague. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this stabbing we have known, so what is plague? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pricking of your enemies of the jinn, and all therein are martyrs. I say: The famous with this chain is from Ziyad, from a man, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2288","Al-Tayalisi said: Musa ibn Bulaydan of the family of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrate from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The stabbed, the castrated, the postpartum woman and the belly-diseased are martyrdom. His father said to him: Did Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrate this to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Thus she narrated to me, and thus I memorized."
"2289","Abu Bakr said: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Badr ibn Uthman, Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to me, from Imran ibn Sad, from his father Sad (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: They are martyred by killing, stabbing, drowning, belly disease, a womans death in childbed together, and her death in her postpartum."
"2290","Abu Yala said: Surayj narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated, Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the cave, and he said: O Allah, stabbing and plague. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I know you have asked the deaths of your nation; this stabbing we have known, so what is plague? He said: Filth like boils; if life prolongs with you, you will see it. Its chain is feeble because of Jafar."
"2291","Abd al-Ala, that is Ibn Hammad, narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Layth, that is Ibn Abi Sulaym, narrate from a companion of his, from Ata: Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Plague was mentioned, and I mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A pricking afflicting my nation from their enemies of the jinn, a swelling like the swelling of the belly; whoever stays upon it is as a frontier guard, and whoever is afflicted by it is a martyr, and whoever flees from it is like the fleer from the battle. Its chain is feeble because of Layth and his shaykh."
"2292","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The martyrs were mentioned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Those who, when they meet the enemy, do not turn their faces until they are killed; those are they who roll in the upper chambers of Paradise, and their Lord laughs to them, and when your Lord laughs to a servant in a place, there is no reckoning upon him."
"2293","Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Salman al-Farisi (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty takes the souls of the martyrs of the sea with His Hand, and does not entrust them to the angel of death, and the likeness of his soul when it leaves his chest is like milk when it enters his chest."
"2294","Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from al-Mughirah ibn Qays, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): al-Mughirah ibn Qays said: And al-Hasan narrated to us part of it, and Qatadah, Said ibn al-Musayyib and al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, he said: And Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), and al-Arzami from Ali ibn Abi Talib, all of them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The martyrs are three: A man who went out with himself and his property, patient, seeking reward, not wanting to kill nor be killed; if he dies or is killed, all his sins are forgiven, he is saved from the punishment of the grave, secured from the greatest terror, married of the houris, a garment of honor is put upon him, and a crown of eternity is placed upon his head. And the second: Went out with himself and his property seeking reward, wanting to kill and not be killed; if he dies or is killed, his knee will be with the knee of Ibrahim, the friend of the Merciful, before Allah, in a seat of truth. And the third: A man who went out with himself and his property seeking reward, wanting to kill and be killed; if he dies or is killed, he will come on the Day of Resurrection brandishing his sword, placing it upon his shoulder, while people are kneeling upon knees, saying: Make way for us, for we have spent our blood for Allah Almighty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, if he said that to Ibrahim or to a prophet among the prophets, he would make way for him from the path, for what he sees of his right; he does not ask Allah Almighty anything except He gives him, and he does not intercede for anyone except intercession is granted for him, and he is given in Paradise what he loves, and no abode of a prophet nor of other than him surpasses him in Paradise, and he has in the Garden of Firdaws a million cities of silver, a million cities of gold, a million cities of pearl, a million cities of ruby, a million cities of durr-pearl, a million cities of chrysolite, and a million cities of light; in every city of the cities, a million palaces; in every palace, a million houses; in every house, a million beds; every bed a thousand years journey in length, a thousand years journey in width, and its height into the sky five hundred years journey; upon it a wife whose sleeve has emerged from the sides of the bed twenty miles from every corner, four corners, the lashes of her eye like the wings of eagles or like the pinions of eagles, her eyebrows like the crescent, upon her garments growing in the Gardens of Eden, her drink from Tasnim, her blossom dazzles sights below her; if she appeared to the people of the world, no sent prophet nor near angel would see her except he would be fascinated by her beauty; before every woman of them a hundred thousand virgin servant girls besides the servants of her husband; before every bed chairs of other than the substance of the bed; every bed a hundred thousand cubits long; upon every bed a hundred thousand mattresses, the thickness of every mattress as between heaven and earth, and what is between them five hundred years journey; they enter Paradise before the truthful and the believers by five hundred years, deflowering virgins; when he draws near the bed, the mattresses lower for him until he mounts them reclining wherever he wishes; he reclines a reclining with the houris seventy years; then one more radiant and beautiful than her calls to him: O servant of Allah, have we no turn from you? He turns to her and says: Who are you? She says: I am of those about whom Allah Almighty said: And with Us is more. Then one more radiant and beautiful calls to him: O servant of Allah, have you no need in us? He says: I did not know your place. She says: Did you not know that Allah Almighty said: No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of eyes. He says: Yes indeed, by my Lord. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps he will be occupied from her after that a year, nothing occupying him except what he is in of bliss and delight. When the people of Paradise enter, the martyrs of the sea ride pearl boats in a river of light, their oars rods of pearl, coral and ruby, with them a wind called al-Zahra in waves like mountains; it is but glittering light; those waves in their eyes are lighter and sweeter to them than cold drink in a white glass to the people of the world on a summer day. And their days which they were at the throats of their companions who were in the world: their boats are advanced before their companions a million years and fifty thousand years, their right flank behind them at half the nearness of those to their companions, their left flank likewise, and their rear guard who were behind them in those pearl boats. While they are thus sailing in that river, those waves raise them to a throne before the Throne of the Lord of Might. While they are thus, the angels appear to them, multiplied over the servants of the people of Paradise in beauty, radiance, loveliness and light, as they are multiplied over the people of Paradise by their stations with Allah. One of them intends to fall prostrate to one of their servants of the angels, and he says: O friend of Allah, I am a servant to you, and we are a hundred thousand stewards in the Gardens of Eden, a hundred thousand stewards in the Gardens of Firdaws, a hundred thousand stewards in the Gardens of Bliss, a hundred thousand stewards in the Gardens of Refuge, a hundred thousand stewards in the Gardens of Eternity, a hundred thousand stewards in the Gardens of the Lawful, and a hundred thousand stewards in the Gardens of Peace; every steward of them over the gate of a city; in every city a hundred thousand palaces; in every palace a hundred thousand houses of gold, silver, durr, ruby, chrysolite, pearl and light; therein his wives, couches and servants; if the lowest of them were visited by jinn and men, and the like of them with them a million times, the lowest palace of his palaces would contain them, whatever they wish of hospitality, servants, fruit, produce, food and drink; every palace self-sufficient with what is in it of these things according to their capacity all; it needs not the other palace in anything of that. And the lowest of them in station is he who enters upon Allah morning and evening, and He commands all honor; he is not occupied until he looks at His beautiful Face, Blessed and Almighty. I say: This is a fabricated hadith; how ignorant is the one who forged it and how audacious against Allah Almighty."
"2295","Abu Yala said: Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad informed me, from Sahl ibn Abi Umamah ibn Hunayf, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of the blood of the martyr to be shed, his every sin is forgiven except debt."
"2296","Chapter 2: Prohibition of applying the name martyr upon mere killing. Al-Harith said: Yahya narrated to us, Shubah narrated, he said: Amr ibn Murrah said: Abu al-Bakhtari al-Tai informed me, he said: Some people were at Kufa with Ibn al-Mukhtar, meaning the father of al-Mukhtar ibn Abi Ubayd, where he was killed at the bridge of Abu Ubayd. He said: They were killed except two men carried upon the enemy with their swords, and they made way for them and they escaped, or three, and they came to Madinah. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went out while they were sitting mentioning them, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: About what did you say to them? They said: We sought forgiveness for them and supplicated for them. He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You shall tell me what you said to them or you shall meet from me conquests. They said: We said: They are martyrs. He said: By Him besides whom there is no god, by Him who sent Muhammad with the truth, by Him besides whose permission the Hour will not stand, no living soul knows what is with Allah for a dead soul, except the Prophet of Allah, for Allah Almighty forgave him what preceded of his sin and what remained. By Him besides whom there is no god, by Him who sent Muhammad with the truth, by Him besides whose permission the Hour will not stand, a man fights for show, and fights for zeal, and fights wanting the world, and fights wanting property, and those who fight have with Allah only what is in their souls. Its men are trustworthy except that it is broken."
"2297","Chapter 3: Intention in jihad. Abu Yala said: Zuhayr, that is Ibn Harb, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, that is Ibn Mahdi, narrated, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated, al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn Rafi narrated to me, Hanan ibn Kharijah narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said to me: O Hanan, begin with yourself and strive against it; O Hanan, begin with yourself and campaign against it; for if you are killed fleeing, Allah will raise you fleeing, and if you are killed showing off, Allah Almighty will raise you showing off, and if you are killed patient seeking reward, Allah Blessed and Almighty will raise you patient seeking reward."
"2298","Abu Yala said: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Amr ibn Shamir narrated, from Jabir al-Jufi, from al-Shabi, from Sasah ibn Sawhan, he said: I heard Zamil ibn Amr al-Judhami narrate from Dhi al-Kala al-Himyari, he said: I heard Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Those slain in fighting will be raised on the Day of Resurrection upon intentions."
"2299","Chapter 4: Prohibition of fighting the Muslim. Musaddad said: Mutamir narrated to us, Awf narrated, a shaykh, I think of Bakr ibn Wail, narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought out a piece of a black woolen garment one day and tied it upon a spear, then shook it and said: Who takes it with its right? The Muslims feared it because of the condition. A man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I take it with its right. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fight with it a Muslim, nor flee with it from a disbeliever."
"2300","Chapter 5: Burying the martyr where he is killed. And Muhammad ibn Abi Umar said: Bishr narrated to us, Said ibn al-Saib al-Taifi narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Miyyah al-Suwai, that two men of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were killed at the gate of Banu Salim, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded they be buried where they were killed. They were carried from where they were struck, and that coincided with a graveyard at Banu Hilal, and they were buried there."
"2301","Chapter 6: Virtue of jihad. Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated, from Abu Muti, Nasr ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from his brother, from Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fights and is patient until he is killed or overcomes is protected from the trial of the grave."
"2302","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Madani narrated, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Aidh, from Amir ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: A man came to prayer while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and said when he reached the row: O Allah, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who is the speaker just now? The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred. Al-Bazzar narrated it from Ahmad ibn Aban and Ahmad ibn Abdah, both from Abd al-Aziz; one of them said from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Aidh, the other from Muslim ibn Aidh. Al-Bazzar said: Muslim or Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated from Amir ibn Sad only this, and it is not narrated from Sad except with this chain."
"2303","Abu Bakr said: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from a shaykh called al-Hafsi, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) called the adhan in the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then called for Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) his life, and did not call in the time of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: What prevents you from calling? He said: I called for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he passed away, and called for Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) until he passed away, because he was my benefactor, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Bilal, there is nothing better than your deed except jihad in the cause of Allah. So he went out to Syria and campaigned."
"2304","And Abd and Abu Yala both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with the same. (83) And the hadith of killing expiating sins except trust will come, Allah willing, in the exegesis of Surat al-Nisa. the hadith of killing expiating sins except trust will come, Allah willing, in the exegesis of Surat al-Nisa."
"2305","Ishaq said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Ukli, from Abu Zurah ibn Umar ibn Jarir, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) sent an army, and among them was Muadh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him). When he marched he saw Muadh (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: What detained you? He said: I wanted to pray Friday then go out. Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A morning going in the cause of Allah Almighty or an evening is better than the world and what is in it."
"2306","Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri narrated to us, Said, that is Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, that is Abu al-Aswad, narrated, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Standing an hour in the cause of Allah Almighty is better than witnessing Laylat al-Qadr at the Black Stone. Abbas al-Tarqufi opposed him, from al-Muqri, and said: From Mujahid instead of Yunus. Ibn Hibban brought it out in his Sahih."
"2307","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, al-Ifriqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum narrated, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whose head is split in the cause of Allah Almighty, Allah forgives him what preceded of his sin."
"2308","And Ibn Abi Umar said: al-Muqri narrated to us. And in the narration of al-Muqri: And he deemed it for reward."
"2309","And Ahmad ibn Mani said: Qurran ibn Tammam and Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, separating them."
"2310","And Abd said: Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us."
"2311","Al-Tayalisi said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed and mentioned jihad, and preferred nothing over it except the prescribed prayer."
"2312","Ahmad ibn Mani said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Kawthar ibn Hakim narrated, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan to Syria, and walked with them about two miles. It was said to him: O successor of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would you turn back? Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whose feet become dusty in the cause of Allah Almighty, Allah Almighty forbids them to the Fire."
"2313","Abu Yala said: Ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A standing of an hour in the cause of Allah is better than a mans worship of sixty years."
"2314","Al-Tayalisi said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Amr, from a man, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with him was a crowd of people, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best in station with Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection after His prophets and His chosen? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The striver in the cause of Allah Almighty with himself and his property until the call of Allah Almighty comes to him while he is upon the back of his horse holding its rein. He said: Then who? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man in a region who perfects the worship of his Lord and spares people his evil."
"2315","Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Maysarah ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated, from Abu Aishah al-Sadi, from Yazid ibn Umar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Huraira and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us. He mentioned the hadith: And whoever stays on frontier or strives in the cause of Allah Almighty will have for every step until he returns seven hundred thousand thousand good deeds, erasure of seven hundred thousand thousand evil deeds, and raising of seven hundred thousand thousand degrees, and he will be in the guarantee of Allah Almighty; if He takes him by whatever death, he will be entered into Paradise, and if He returns him, He returns him forgiven and answered. This is a fabricated hadith."
"2316","And he also said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urged us to jihad and said: The likeness of the strivers of my nation is like the likeness of Jibril and Mikail, and they are the messengers of Allah Blessed and Almighty and His treasurers."
"2317","Dawud narrated to us, Abbad narrated, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and from a man, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says a takbir in the cause of Allah Almighty will have thereby a rock in his scale on the Day of Resurrection heavier than the seven heavens and the seven earths and what is in them, between them and under them. And whoever says in the cause of Allah: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and raises his voice with it, Allah Almighty writes for him His greatest pleasure; and whoever Allah Almighty writes for him His greatest pleasure joins him with Ibrahim and Muhammad (peace and blessings upon them) in the abode of majesty. It was said: What is the abode of majesty? He said: The abode of Allah Almighty which He named Himself by; he looks to the Possessor of majesty and honor morning and evening. That is forbidden to the killer of the believing soul, and the disobedient to parents; they are free of me, and I am free of them."
"2318","Abu Bakr said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, he said: Yazid ibn Shajarah stood among his companions and said: It has become upon you and eveninged from among red, green and yellow, and in graves is what is therein; when you meet the enemy tomorrow, forward, forward. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man advances a step except the houris advance to him; if he retreats they retreat, and if he is martyred, his first spurt is expiation of his sins, and two of the houris descend to him and shake off the dust from him, saying: Welcome, it is time for you, and he says: Welcome, it is time for you two."
"2319","And Abd said: Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us with the same."
"2320","Abu Yala said: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated, from Ali ibn Ali, Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, that he narrated to him, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Buy upon Allah and borrow upon Allah. It was said: Who borrows upon Allah, O Messenger of Allah? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your saying: Lend us until our livelihood, and sell us until Allah opens for us. You will remain in good as long as your jihad remains. There will be in the end of time a people who doubt in jihad; so strive in their time and campaign, for campaigning that day is better."
"2321","1947 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Jamil ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sets out for Hajj and dies, the reward of the pilgrim is written for him until the Day of Resurrection; and whoever sets out as a warrior in the path of Allah Most High and dies, the reward of the warrior is written for him until the Day of Resurrection; and whoever sets out for Umrah and dies, the reward of the one performing Umrah is written for him until the Day of Resurrection."
"2322","1948 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Hilali narrated to us, from Tawus and Makhul, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An hour in the path of Allah Most High is better than fifty pilgrimages."
"2323","1949 - Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Habib ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day he addressed the people: There is none among people like a man who takes hold of his horse's head and strives in the path of Allah and avoids the evils of people, and like a man settled in comfort who honors his guest and gives his due."
"2324","1950 - And Abd said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abi Farwah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed is an expiation for every sin except shirk."
"2325","1951 - And Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Amr ibn Safwan narrated to us, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning or evening journey in the path of Allah is better than this world and what is in it."
"2326","Chapter 7: The virtue of ribat and its superiority over worship. 1952/1 - Al-Tayalisi said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from As'as ibn Salamah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and missed a man from his Companions, and he was brought to him, and he said: I intended to be alone in worship of my Lord and withdraw from people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do it, and let none of you do it - he said it three times - for enduring a single hour in one of the stations of the Muslims is better than worship of forty years."
"2327","1952/2 - And al-Harith said: Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Azraq ibn Qays saying: I heard As'as ibn Salamah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his journey, and he mentioned it."
"2328","1953 - Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ribat of a day in the path of Allah equals worship of a month or a year, its fasting and its standing in prayer; and whoever dies guarding the frontier in the path of Allah Most High, Allah Most High protects him from the punishment of the grave and continues his reward of ribat for him as long as this world lasts."
"2329","Chapter 8: Prohibition of killing women, children, traders, delegations and messengers. 1954/1 - Ishaq said: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik or Abd Allah ibn Ka'b - and he was the guide of Ka'b ibn Malik - from Ka'b ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to us when we were at Khaybar: Do not kill a child or a woman. This is an authentic chain."
"2330","1954/2 - Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me, from his uncle (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them to Ibn Abi al-Huqayq, he forbade them from killing women and children."
"2331","1955 - Musaddad said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, he said: A man came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and knelt on his knees, and praised Allah Most High and repeated the praise with him three times, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fight him; what a word Satan poured upon him? And if I were to kill a delegation from the Arabs, I would have killed him. It is mursal with an authentic chain."
"2332","1956/1 - And Abu Bakr said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hajjaj - he is Ibn Artah - from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We did not kill the traders of the polytheists in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2333","1956/2 - Abu Ya'la narrated it from Abu Bakr with it."
"2334","1957 - And Abu Ya'la said: Ahmad ibn Isa al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed me, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition he said: In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); do not steal from the spoils, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill children."
"2335","Chapter 9: Encouragement to assist the fighters. 1958 - Al-Harith said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah Most High has fought, and whoever looks after a warrior's family well has fought."
"2336","Chapter 10: Virtue of one who sees off a fighter. 1959 - Al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Salman al-Farisi (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees off a party going out in the path of Allah Most High until they settle at the first stop and stays the night with them until they depart heading for jihad, then returns until he reaches his family, he has the reward of seventy pilgrimages with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), besides sharing with them in whatever good they are in."
"2337","1960 - Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Dharr, similar to it; but he said: As if he performed twenty-five pilgrimages, instead of seventy."
"2338","1961 - And Ahmad ibn Mani' said: Abu Nasr al-Tammar Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Kawthar ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan to Sham, and walked with them about two miles, and it was said to him: O successor of the Messenger of Allah, if only you would turn back? So Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whosever two feet become dusty in the path of Allah Most High, Allah Mighty and Majestic forbids them both from the Fire. Al-Bazzar narrated it from Amr ibn Ali from Abu Nasr al-Tammar with the raised chain."
"2339","Chapter 11: Banners and standards. 1962 - Abu Ya'la said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hayyan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Abu Mijlaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said; and Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was black, and his standard was white."
"2340","1963 - Ismail ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman of the family of Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Kilab, he said: He heard Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Mighty and Majestic honored my nation with banners."
"2341","Chapter 12: Etiquette of travel and companionship. 1964 - Musaddad said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar, from a man of the Ansar, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade farewell to a man and said: May Allah provide you with piety, forgive your sin, and make good easy for you wherever you are."
"2342","1965 - And Abu Ya'la said: Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Ulathah narrated to us, from Wasil the freed slave of Abu Uyaynah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked, when he intended a journey, to set out on Thursday. Amr ibn al-Husayn is abandoned."
"2343","1966/1 - And Abu Bakr said: Waki' narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place, he did not depart from it until he bade it farewell with two rak'ahs."
"2344","1966/2 - And Abu Ya'la said: Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, my father narrated to us with it, except that he said: When he traveled."
"2345","1967 - And Musaddad said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Ayyub narrating from Abu Qilabah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was gentle among the people, and there was in a group among those groups a man whose companions called out to him, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, when we stopped he prayed, and when we traveled he recited. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then who provided fodder for his camel? They said: We did. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of you are better than him, or as he said. This is a good mursal."
"2346","1968 - And Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', that he heard Mujahid narrating from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): When he intended that a man accompany him on his journey, he stipulated that he not accompany us on an unlawfully owned camel, that he not dispute the call to prayer with us, and that he not fast except with our permission. Nafi' said: A man used to accompany him on travel, and he would order us to wake him and prepare his predawn meal for him."
"2347","1969 - And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Abd Allah al-Shaqari, from Salman al-Farisi (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever serves twelve men in the path of Allah Most High emerges from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him, and whoever gives drink to a man in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic will come to the Basin of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Resurrection. He said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled with them, he stipulated service upon the best of them, and whoever missed that, he stipulated the call to prayer; he said: A people came as a delegation to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a battle, and he saw among them people exhausted by worship, and said: Who used to serve them? Some of them said: We did, O Messenger of Allah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are better than them."
"2348","1970 - And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Hammam narrated to us, Sa'id al-Zubaydi narrated to me, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Awsabi narrated to me, Abu Abd Allah al-Dimashqi narrated to me, he said: I heard Aktham ibn al-Jawn al-Khuza'i al-Ka'bi saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Aktham ibn al-Jawn, go out to fight with other than your people; your character will improve and you will be honored by your companions."
"2349","1971 - And with it he said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of companions are four, the hadith."
"2350","1972 - And al-Harith said: Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Uyaynah, a man of the people of Madinah informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd ibn Harithah or to Amr ibn al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both): When you send an expedition, do not corrupt them and bring them down gently; for Allah Most High grants the people victory through their weakest."
"2351","1973 - Al-Harith said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq - he is al-Fazari - narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from a man of Juhaynah, from a man, he said: We fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw a stopping place that was narrow, so the people crowded and cut off the road, so his caller announced: Whoever blocks a dwelling place or cuts off a road has no jihad."
"2352","Chapter 13: Virtue of the comfortable mount. 1974 - Ishaq said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Of a person's happiness are three: a righteous wife, a good mount, and a spacious dwelling; and of a person's wretchedness: a bad wife, a bad mount, and a narrow dwelling."
"2353","1975 - Abu Bakr said: Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, he said: I heard Ibn Qurrah - or Qurrah, Abu Bakr doubted - that he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three are of the bliss of this world, though it has no real bliss: a comfortable mount, a righteous wife, and a spacious dwelling."
"2354","Chapter 15: Prohibition of a woman traveling alone. 1976 - Abu Ya'la said: Sulayman ibn Yazid, the freed slave of Banu Hashim at Basra, narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid al-Suda'i narrated to us, from Abu Hani', from Amir, from Adi ibn Hatim (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not travel more than three days except with a husband or a mahram."
"2355","Chapter 16: Kindness to animals. 1977 - Abu Bakr said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: I heard Ammar ibn Abi Ammar saying: Honor the goats, wipe the mucus from them, and pray in their resting place; for they are of the animals of Paradise. It is mawquf, authentic."
"2356","1978 - And al-Harith said: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, he said: Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by people who had made a camel kneel and loaded it with two sacks, then added another on top of it so the camel could not rise, so Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) threw it off from it then made it stand, and Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If Allah forgives you for what you do to beasts, He will forgive something great; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Most High enjoins upon you good toward these speechless creatures, that you make them stop at their proper places, and when a year of drought strikes you, that you move off them with their fat. Ahmad narrated it from another route from Abu Idris al-Khawlani from Abu al-Darda, raised: If you were forgiven for what you do to beasts, much would be forgiven for you."
"2357","1979 - And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ami'rah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the back of every camel is a devil, so when you ride them mention Allah, and treat them humbly; for it is Allah Mighty and Majestic who carries."
"2358","1980 - And Abu Ya'la said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Sayfi ibn Rib'i narrated to us, from Umar ibn Musa al-Ansari, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa', from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave camels untied and tie their udders firmly; for Satan suckles them."
"2359","1981 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Qari narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, he said: Anas informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the land is fertile, dismount from your backs and give it its right of grazing, and when the land is barren, travel swiftly upon it with its fat. Al-Bazzar said: We do not know of anyone who narrated it from al-Layth except Ruwaym ibn Yazid, and it was narrated from al-Zuhri as mursal."
"2360","1982 - Abu Ya'la said: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Farewell Pilgrimage and he took his wives out with him; she said: My baggage was light, and I was on a swift camel, and the baggage of Safiyyah bint Huyayy had weight - the hadith; and it has already come in the Book of Marriage."
"2361","Chapter 17: Horses, their virtue, encouragement to treat them well, and virtue of carrying upon them in the path of Allah. 1983/1 - Al-Tayalisi said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind al-Ashja'i narrated to me, he said: He was seen wiping the cheek of his horse, and he was asked about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril (peace be upon him) reproached me concerning the horse."
"2362","1983/2 - And Yunus ibn Habib the narrator from Abu Dawud said: Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Urwah al-Bariqi."
"2363","1984 - And Musaddad said: Yahya narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from a man of the Ansar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up wiping the sweat of his horse, and he was asked, and he said: I was reproached last night concerning horses."
"2364","1985 - And Abd said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Salit ibn Yasar ibn Salit ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Maryam bint Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Umm Sa'd bint Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' - and she is the mother of Kharijah ibn Zayd - from Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever keeps a horse in the path of Allah Most High, it will be his screen from the Fire."
"2365","1986 - And al-Harith said: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Zur'ah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from his grandfather Jarir, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping the face of his horse with his sleeve. Ahmad narrated it from the route of Hushaym from Yunus with the wording: Twisting the forelock of a horse with his finger. Perhaps they are two hadiths. Hadith 85: Satan does not frighten anyone in a house in which there is an aged horse - in Surah al-Anfal."
"2366","1987 - And Abu Ya'la said: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Ali, Yunus narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, that he narrated to him, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man came to him and said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying anything about horses? He said: Yes, I heard him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"2367","1988 - And Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Ismail ibn Sa'id al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Ubayd al-Jubayri, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and their people are aided upon them."
"2368","Chapter 18: Share of the horseman. 1989 - Al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Aflah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Abi Ahmad, that he heard Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted two shares for the horse and one share for its owner."
"2369","1990 - Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Yahya ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying the like of it."
"2370","1991 - And al-Harith said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from his aunt Quraybah, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr, from al-Miqdad ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned him on the day of Badr two shares for his horse and one share for him."
"2371","1992 - Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hathmah, he said: He witnessed Hunayn with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he allotted two shares for his horse and one share for him."
"2372","1993 - Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ghatfan, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: For the horse is one share, for the Arabian and the non-Arabian alike."
"2373","1994 - And Muhammad ibn Umar said: Abd Allah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I asked Ikrimah (may Allah be pleased with him) about that, he said: They are alike."
"2374","1995 - Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Aban ibn Salih, from Ata ibn Yasar, the like of it."
"2375","1996 - Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, they both said: They are alike in the two shares, meaning the Arabian and the mixed breed."
"2376","1997 - And Abu Ya'la said: Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abi Farwah, that Abu Hazim the freed slave of Abu Ruhm informed him, from Abu Ruhm and his brother: That they were two horsemen on the day of Hunayn, and they were given six shares: four for their two horses, and two for themselves, and they sold the two shares for two young camels."
"2377","1998 - Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave on the day of Badr the horse two shares and the man one share."
"2378","Chapter 19: Racing, shooting, and what has come on the virtue of shooting. 1999 - Abu Ya'la said: Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Darawardi narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Ishaq ibn Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who gathers horses on the day of racing, and he is not of us who stirs a slave against his master, and he is not of us who corrupts a wife against her husband."
"2379","2000/1 - And Abu Bakr and Ahmad ibn Mani' both said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from Abu Rashid, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inspected the people and saw a man with an Arabian bow in his hand, and said: Stick to this and its like, and the spears of the lances; for by this Allah Most High will establish you in lands and support you in victory."
"2380","2000/2 - And al-Tayalisi said: Ash'ath ibn Sa'id - he is Abu al-Rabi' al-Samman - narrated to us with this."
"2381","2001 - And Musaddad said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Kathir narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced between horses and camels."
"2382","2002 - And Abu Bakr said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting and said: Take, and I am with Ibn al-Adra'. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we take while you are with some of us and not others? So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take, and I am with you, O sons of Ismail."
"2383","2003 - Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people of Aslam competing in shooting, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was a shooter, and I am with Ibn al-Akwa'. So the people held back their hands, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not shoot? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we shoot while you said: I am with Ibn al-Akwa', and we know your party is not beaten. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shoot, and I am with all of you."
"2384","2004 - And al-Harith said: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Fight the people of disbelief; whoever reaches with an arrow has a degree. It was said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what is the degree? He said: What is between the heaven and the earth."
"2385","2005 - And Abd ibn Humayd said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Salim ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Abd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: For every Muslim are three: There is no man of the Muslims who shoots an arrow in the path of Allah Most High at the enemy, whether it hits or misses, except the reward of that arrow is for him like freeing a slave; and there is no man of the Muslims whose hair turns white in the path of Allah Most High except it will be a light running before him on the Day of Resurrection; and there is no man of the Muslims who frees a young or old slave except it is right upon Allah Most High to reward him manifold for every limb of him."
"2386","2006 - And Musaddad said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Abi Dawud, from a shaykh of the people of Madinah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to shoot with an arrow except one he can see."
"2387","2007 - Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he saw no harm in two men betting on racing, and he disliked that they separate over that."
"2388","2008 - Yahya ibn Sa'id - meaning al-Qattan - narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: There is no harm in betting on horses when there is among them a horse that is not below them: if it wins, the prize is his, and if it does not win, nothing is upon him."
"2389","Chapter 20: Intensity of running and walking. 2009 - Ishaq said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father, he said: I came hastening as fast as the wind, and passed by a group of the Ansar near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I never saw before them nor after them like them - wearing swords, nearly thirty, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have seen fear."
"2390","2010 - Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: People complained to the Messenger of Allah about walking, so he called them and said: Upon you is brisk walking; so we walked briskly and found it lighter upon us."
"2391","2011 - Abu Ya'la said: Abu Musa narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Mu'awiyah narrating from Ibn Abd al-Shariq al-Khath'ami, from Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant's two feet become dusty in the path of Allah Most High except Allah forbids the Fire for him; and I never saw more walking than that day when we were behind the mountain pass."
"2392","Chapter 21: Command to improve weapons and prepare them for jihad. 2012 - Musaddad said: Isa - he is Ibn Yunus - narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from his teachers, he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Keep your nails long in the land of the enemy, for they are a weapon. It is mawquf, disconnected."
"2393","Chapter 22: Prohibition of breeding a donkey onto an Arabian mare. 2013 - Musaddad said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote: Any man of the people of the register who breeds a donkey onto an Arabian mare, deduct ten dinars from his stipend."
"2394","2014 - And Abu Ya'la said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a donkey called Ufayr."
"2395","Chapter 23: Supplication at meeting the enemy and command of silence. 2015 - Al-Harith said: al-Sakan ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the enemy he said: O Allah, You are my support and my helper; by You I move, by You I attack, and by You I fight. I said: Abu Dawud brought it fuller from the hadith of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and it is with al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i also, all of them from the narration of Abu Sa'id from Qatadah from him; and I saw in a copy: from Abu Mijlaz from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him); on this basis it is not to be held against him."
"2396","2016 - Abu Ya'la said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Ruhm, from a man, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Most High loves silence at three times: at the recitation of the Qur'an, at the battle line, and at the funeral."
"2397","Chapter 24: War cries. 2017 - Abu Ya'la said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The war cry of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O source of all good."
"2398","Chapter 25: Calling to Islam before fighting. Hadith 86 will come, Allah willing, in the Book of Leadership, in the chapter of how covenants are entrusted to commanders: The letter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, and in it is what belongs here. 2018 - Ishaq said: Waki' informed us, from Umar ibn Dharr, from Yahya ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Talhah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him on a mission, then said to a man: Catch up with him and do not startle him from behind him, and say to him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to wait for him, and say to him: Do not fight a people until you call them."
"2399","2019/1 - And Musaddad said: Yahya - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Thawr, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition he said: Befriend the people and be gentle with them, and do not raid them until you call them; for there is no household of town-dwellers or tent-dwellers on earth but that your bringing them to me as Muslims is dearer to me than your killing their men and bringing me their women."
"2400","2019/2 - And al-Harith said: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, and he mentioned the like of it, and he did not mention Abd al-Rahman in his chain."
